<li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_timelines#Science" title="List of timelines">List of science timelines</a></li></ul></td>
</tr><tr><td class="sidebar-navbar"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333133064" about="#mwt3349" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Hlist/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239400231" about="#mwt3350" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Navbar/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div class="navbar plainlinks hlist navbar-mini"><ul><li class="nv-view"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Science_decade_nav" title="Template:Science decade nav"><abbr title="View this template">v</abbr></a></li><li class="nv-talk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Science_decade_nav" title="Template talk:Science decade nav"><abbr title="Discuss this template">t</abbr></a></li><li class="nv-edit"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:EditPage/Template:Science_decade_nav" title="Special:EditPage/Template:Science decade nav"><abbr title="Edit this template">e</abbr></a></li></ul></div></td></tr></tbody></table>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3351" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwKeI" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2020s in science and technology&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt3352" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt3351" id="mwKeM">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020s_in_science_and_technology" title="2020s in science and technology">2020s in science and technology</a></div>

<p id="mwKeQ">Below are the most significant scientific developments of each year, based on the annual Breakthrough of the Year award of the American Association for the Advancement of Science journal Science.</p>

<ul id="mwKeU"><li id="mwKeY">2020: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_vaccine" title="COVID-19 vaccine" id="mwKec">COVID-19 vaccine</a>, developed and tested at record speed<sup about="#mwt3355" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-892" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-892&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-892" id="mwKeg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKek"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKeo">[</span>892<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKes">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwKew">2021: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaFold" title="AlphaFold" id="mwKe0">An AI</a> brings <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protein_structure_prediction" title="Protein structure prediction" id="mwKe4">protein structures</a> to all<sup about="#mwt3358" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-893" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-893&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-893" id="mwKe8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKfA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKfE">[</span>893<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKfI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwKfM">2022: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Webb_Space_Telescope" title="James Webb Space Telescope" id="mwKfQ">James Webb Space Telescope</a> debut<sup about="#mwt3361" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-894" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-894&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-894" id="mwKfU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKfY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKfc">[</span>894<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKfg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwKfk">2023: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GLP-1_receptor_agonist" title="GLP-1 receptor agonist" id="mwKfo">GLP-1 Drugs</a> anorectic drugs<sup about="#mwt3364" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-895" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-895&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-895" id="mwKfs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKfw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKf0">[</span>895<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKf4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwKf8">2024: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lenacapavir" title="Lenacapavir" id="mwKgA">Lenacapavir</a> antiretroviral medication used to treat and prevent HIV/AIDS<sup about="#mwt3367" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-896" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-896&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-896" id="mwKgE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKgI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKgM">[</span>896<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKgQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<section data-mw-section-id="41" id="mwKgU" aria-labelledby="Artificial_intelligence"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Artificial_intelligence">Artificial intelligence</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=41" title="Edit section: Artificial intelligence"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwKgY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Timeline-of-AI-generated-faces.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwKgc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Timeline-of-AI-generated-faces.png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Timeline-of-AI-generated-faces.png/120px-Timeline-of-AI-generated-faces.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="8245" data-file-height="9340" data-file-type="bitmap" height="136" width="120" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Timeline-of-AI-generated-faces.png/250px-Timeline-of-AI-generated-faces.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwKgg"></a><figcaption id="mwKgk">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_boom" title="AI boom" id="mwKgo">AI boom</a> emerged in the 2020s. Generative AI such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Text-to-image_model" title="Text-to-image model" id="mwKgs">Text-to-image models</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatGPT" title="ChatGPT" id="mwKgw">AI chatbots</a> released publicly. Machine learning systems that took minute(s) to produce blurry images in mid 2022 were able to produce more realistic imagery in seconds by mid 2023. English text would appear as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibberish" title="Gibberish" id="mwKg0">gibberish</a> in earlier AI text-to-image builds, although this was fixed to an extent with newer AI models such as DALL-E 3.</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwKg4">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_boom" title="AI boom" id="mwKg8">AI boom</a><sup about="#mwt3370" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-897" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-897&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-897" id="mwKhA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKhE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKhI">[</span>897<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKhM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3373" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-898" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-898&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-898" id="mwKhQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKhU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKhY">[</span>898<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKhc">]</span></span></a></sup> is an ongoing period of rapid <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Progress_in_artificial_intelligence" title="Progress in artificial intelligence" id="mwKhg">progress in</a> the field of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence" title="Artificial intelligence" id="mwKhk">artificial intelligence</a> (AI) that started in the late 2010s before gaining international prominence throughout the 2020s with the public release of consumer-facing chatbots such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatGPT" title="ChatGPT" id="mwKho">ChatGPT</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeepSeek" title="DeepSeek" id="mwKhs">DeepSeek</a>.<sup about="#mwt3376" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-899" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-899&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-899" id="mwKhw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKh0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKh4">[</span>899<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKh8">]</span></span></a></sup> Examples include <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_language_model" title="Large language model" id="mwKiA">large language models</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_AI" title="Generative AI" id="mwKiE">generative AI</a> applications developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenAI" title="OpenAI" id="mwKiI">OpenAI</a> as well as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protein_structure_prediction" title="Protein structure prediction" id="mwKiM">protein folding prediction</a> led by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_DeepMind" title="Google DeepMind" id="mwKiQ">Google DeepMind</a>. This period is sometimes referred to as an <b id="mwKiU">AI spring</b>, to contrast it with previous <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_winter" title="AI winter" id="mwKiY">AI winters</a>.<sup about="#mwt3379" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-900" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-900&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-900" id="mwKic"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKig"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKik">[</span>900<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKio">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3382" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-901" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-901&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-901" id="mwKis"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKiw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKi0">[</span>901<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKi4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<ul id="mwKi8"><li id="mwKjA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeepMind" title="DeepMind" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKjE">DeepMind</a> solves the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protein_folding_problem" title="Protein folding problem" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKjI">protein folding problem</a> to 90 percent accuracy, a 50-year-old grand challenge, at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CASP" title="CASP" id="mwKjM">CASP</a>14 in 2020.<sup about="#mwt3385" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-902" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-902&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-902" id="mwKjQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKjU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKjY">[</span>902<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKjc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3388" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-903" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-903&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-903" id="mwKjg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKjk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKjo">[</span>903<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKjs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwKjw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Text-to-image_model" title="Text-to-image model" id="mwKj0">Text-to-image AI art systems</a> such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DALL-E" title="DALL-E" id="mwKj4">DALL-E</a> (1, 2, and 3) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stable_Diffusion" title="Stable Diffusion" id="mwKj8">Stable Diffusion</a> are capable of generating highly detailed and realistic images from text <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prompt_engineering" title="Prompt engineering" id="mwKkA">prompts</a>.</li>
<li id="mwKkE">Chatbots using <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fine-tuning_(deep_learning)" title="Fine-tuning (deep learning)" id="mwKkI">fine-tuned</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_language_model" title="Large language model" id="mwKkM">large language models</a>, like <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenAI" title="OpenAI" id="mwKkQ">OpenAI</a>'s <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatGPT" title="ChatGPT" id="mwKkU">ChatGPT</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthropic" title="Anthropic" id="mwKkY">Anthropic</a>'s <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_(language_model)" title="Claude (language model)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKkc">Claude</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_Platforms" title="Meta Platforms" id="mwKkg">Meta's</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Llama_(language_model)" title="Llama (language model)" id="mwKkk">Llama</a>, became widely adopted in 2023 and 2024.<sup about="#mwt3391" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-904" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-904&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-904" id="mwKko"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKks"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKkw">[</span>904<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKk0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwKk4">In early 2024, OpenAI released a new technology called <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sora_(text-to-video_model)" title="Sora (text-to-video model)" id="mwKk8">Sora</a>, a video model that generates short video clips based on user prompts, and can also extend existing short videos. Sora was released publicly for ChatGPT Plus and ChatGPT Pro users in December 2024. This has revolutionized the video industry, since this machine generates videos in shorter time, leading to more companies adopting AI videos, with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coca-Cola" title="Coca-Cola" id="mwKlA">Coca-Cola</a> being the first one to do so.<sup about="#mwt3394" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-905" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-905&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-905" id="mwKlE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKlI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKlM">[</span>905<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKlQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3397" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-906" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-906&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-906" id="mwKlU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKlY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKlc">[</span>906<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKlg">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="42" id="mwKlk" aria-labelledby="Communications_and_electronics"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Communications_and_electronics">Communications and electronics</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=42" title="Edit section: Communications and electronics"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwKlo"><li id="mwKls"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5G" title="5G" id="mwKlw">5G</a> became increasingly widespread during the decade.</li>
<li id="mwKl0">By 2020, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3D_printing" title="3D printing" id="mwKl4">3D printing</a> had reached decent quality and affordable pricing which allowed many people to own 3D printers.</li>
<li id="mwKl8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8K_resolution" title="8K resolution" id="mwKmA">8K resolution</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4K_resolution" title="4K resolution" id="mwKmE">4K resolution</a> becomes prevalent in consumer electronics.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="43" id="mwKmI" aria-labelledby="Spaceflight"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Spaceflight">Spaceflight</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=43" title="Edit section: Spaceflight"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3398" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwKmM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;See also&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:See_also&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2020s in spaceflight&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt3399" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt3398" id="mwKmQ">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020s_in_spaceflight" title="2020s in spaceflight">2020s in spaceflight</a></div>

<p id="mwKmU">The trend towards cost reduction in access to orbit is expected to continue. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vulcan_Centaur" title="Vulcan Centaur" id="mwKmY">Vulcan</a> is replacing its more expensive predecessors.<sup about="#mwt3402" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-907" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-907&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-907" id="mwKmc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKmg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKmk">[</span>907<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKmo">]</span></span></a></sup> Since 2023, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SpaceX" title="SpaceX" id="mwKms">SpaceX</a> is testing its fully reusable <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SpaceX_Starship" title="SpaceX Starship" id="mwKmw">Starship</a> with orbital missions.<sup about="#mwt3405" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-908" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-908&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-908" id="mwKm0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKm4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKm8">[</span>908<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKnA">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2025, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Origin" title="Blue Origin" id="mwKnE">Blue Origin</a> conducted the maiden flight of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Glenn" title="New Glenn" id="mwKnI">New Glenn</a> with a reusable first stage and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ariane_6" title="Ariane 6" id="mwKnM">Ariane 6</a> replaced the, retired more expensive, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ariane_5" title="Ariane 5" id="mwKnQ">Ariane 5</a>.<sup about="#mwt3408" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-909" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-909&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-909" id="mwKnU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKnY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKnc">[</span>909<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKng">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwKnk">Mars stays a focus for missions to other planets, with three missions launched in 2020 (by China, the United Arab Emirates and the United States) and at least one mission planned for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EscaPADE" title="EscaPADE" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKno">2024</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martian_Moons_eXploration" title="Martian Moons eXploration" id="mwKns">2026</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosalind_Franklin_(rover)" title="Rosalind Franklin (rover)" id="mwKnw">2028</a>.<sup about="#mwt3411" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-910" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-910&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-910" id="mwKn0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKn4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKn8">[</span>910<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKoA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwKoE">In 2028, as part of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NASA-ESA_Mars_Sample_Return" title="NASA-ESA Mars Sample Return" id="mwKoI">NASA-ESA Mars Sample Return</a> mission, NASA plans to launch a Sample Retrieval Lander. In 2027, ESA plans to launch the Earth Return Orbiter, which will transport the retrieved samples from Mars to Earth by 2033. China is also planning to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars_sample-return_mission#China" title="Mars sample-return mission" id="mwKoM">retrieve samples from Mars</a> by 2031.<sup about="#mwt3414" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-911" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-911&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-911" id="mwKoQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKoU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKoY">[</span>911<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKoc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwKog">NASA plans a return of humans to the Moon by 2028. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemis_I" title="Artemis I" id="mwKok">first uncrewed launch</a> of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Launch_System" title="Space Launch System" id="mwKoo">Space Launch System</a> happened in 2022.<sup about="#mwt3417" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-912" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-912&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-912" id="mwKos"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKo0">[</span>912<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKo4">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemis_II" title="Artemis II" id="mwKo8">The first crewed launch</a>, a lunar flyby, occurred in April 2026.<sup about="#mwt3420" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sn-20240109_913-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;sn-20240109&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-sn-20240109-913&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-sn-20240109-913" id="mwKpA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKpE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKpI">[</span>913<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKpM">]</span></span></a></sup> NASA is aiming toward <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemis_IV" title="Artemis IV" id="mwKpQ">a 2028 lunar landing</a>.</p>

<p id="mwKpU">India plans to launch its first crewed flight with a spacecraft called <i id="mwKpY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaganyaan" title="Gaganyaan" id="mwKpc">Gaganyaan</a></i> on a home-grown <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GSLV_Mark_III" title="GSLV Mark III" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKpg">GSLV Mark III</a> rocket in 2025. The mission would make India the fourth nation to launch a crewed spaceflight after Russia, the US and China. India also plans to launch its second Mars probe, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars_Orbiter_Mission_2" title="Mars Orbiter Mission 2" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKpk">Mars Orbiter Mission 2</a> (<i id="mwKpo">Mangalyaan 2</i>).<sup about="#mwt3423" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-914" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-914&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-914" id="mwKps"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKpw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKp0">[</span>914<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKp4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwKp8">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Webb_Space_Telescope" title="James Webb Space Telescope" id="mwKqA">James Webb Space Telescope</a> was launched in 2021. NASA plans to launch the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nancy_Grace_Roman_Space_Telescope" title="Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope" id="mwKqE">Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope</a>, which will have a field of view 100 times larger than that of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hubble_Space_Telescope" title="Hubble Space Telescope" id="mwKqI">Hubble Space Telescope</a>, no earlier than September 2026.<sup about="#mwt3426" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nasa-20220719_915-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;nasa-20220719&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-nasa-20220719-915&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-nasa-20220719-915" id="mwKqM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKqQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKqU">[</span>915<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKqY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3429" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sn-20210930_916-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;sn-20210930&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-sn-20210930-916&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-sn-20210930-916" id="mwKqc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKqg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKqk">[</span>916<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKqo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3432" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sn20200520_917-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;sn20200520&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-sn20200520-917&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-sn20200520-917" id="mwKqs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKqw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKq0">[</span>917<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKq4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3435" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-918" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-918&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-918" id="mwKq8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKrA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKrE">[</span>918<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKrI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwKrM">NASA's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NEO_Surveyor" title="NEO Surveyor" id="mwKrQ">NEO Surveyor</a>, scheduled to launch no later than June 2028,<sup about="#mwt3439" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sn-20221207_919-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;sn-20221207&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-sn-20221207-919&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-sn-20221207-919" id="mwKrU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKrY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKrc">[</span>919<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKrg">]</span></span></a></sup> is expected to be capable of detecting at least 90% of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Near-Earth_object" title="Near-Earth object" id="mwKrk">near-Earth objects</a> larger than <span about="#mwt3436" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwKro" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;convert&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Convert&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;140&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;m&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ft&quot;},&quot;sp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;us&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">140 meters (460</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt3436">&nbsp;</span><span about="#mwt3436">ft)</span>, a goal mandated by the US Congress in 2005.<sup about="#mwt3442" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-920" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-920&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-920" id="mwKrs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKrw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKr0">[</span>920<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKr4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwKr8">The number of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Small_satellites" title="Small satellites" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKsA">small satellites</a> launched annually was expected to grow to around one thousand (2018 estimate), mainly <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satellite_constellation#Communications_satellite_constellations" title="Satellite constellation" id="mwKsE">communication satellites in large constellations</a><sup about="#mwt3445" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-921" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-921&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-921" id="mwKsI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKsM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKsQ">[</span>921<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKsU">]</span></span></a></sup> but launches quickly exceeded this estimate, mainly due to the rapid deployment of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starlink" title="Starlink" id="mwKsY">Starlink</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OneWeb" title="OneWeb" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKsc">OneWeb</a> constellations. From 2020 to 2022, around 3500 Starlink satellites<sup about="#mwt3448" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-922" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-922&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-922" id="mwKsg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKsk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKso">[</span>922<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKss">]</span></span></a></sup> and 500 satellites by OneWeb<sup about="#mwt3451" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-923" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-923&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-923" id="mwKsw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKs0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKs4">[</span>923<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKs8">]</span></span></a></sup> were launched.</p>

<p id="mwKtA">The number of total satellites reached 10,000 for the first time in 2024.<sup about="#mwt3454" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-924" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-924&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-924" id="mwKtE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKtI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKtM">[</span>924<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKtQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="44" id="mwKtU" aria-labelledby="Software_and_electronic_platforms"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Software_and_electronic_platforms">Software and electronic platforms</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=44" title="Edit section: Software and electronic platforms"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwKtY"><li id="mwKtc">Support for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe_Flash_Player" title="Adobe Flash Player" id="mwKtg">Adobe Flash Player</a> ended on 31 December 2020.</li>
<li id="mwKtk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_11" title="Windows 11" id="mwKto">Windows 11</a> is released on 5 October 2021, succeeding <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_10" title="Windows 10" id="mwKts">Windows 10</a>.</li>
<li id="mwKtw">Support for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Explorer" title="Internet Explorer" id="mwKt0">Internet Explorer</a> on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_10" title="Windows 10" id="mwKt4">Windows 10</a> Semi-Annual Channel (SAC) ended on 15 June 2022.</li>
<li id="mwKt8">ESU support for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_7" title="Windows 7" id="mwKuA">Windows 7</a> and extended support for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_8.1" title="Windows 8.1" id="mwKuE">Windows 8.1</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_RT" title="Windows RT" id="mwKuI">Windows RT</a> ended on 10 January 2023. Some versions of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_10" title="Windows 10" id="mwKuM">Windows 10</a>, such as Windows 10 2106 LTSB are already out of <i id="mwKuQ">mainstream</i> support, some versions <!-- e.g. all Mobile --> are out of all support, and others soon on, i.e. 14 October 2025, while some Enterprise versions will be supported longer.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="45" id="mwKuU" aria-labelledby="Technology"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Technology">Technology</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=45" title="Edit section: Technology"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwKuY"><li id="mwKuc">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BBC" title="BBC" id="mwKug">BBC</a> reports that for the "first time someone who has had a complete cut to their spinal cord has been able to walk freely... because of an electrical implant that has been surgically attached to his spine".<sup about="#mwt3457" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-925" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-925&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-925" id="mwKuk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKuo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKus">[</span>925<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKuw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwKu0">Sales of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_vehicle" title="Electric vehicle" id="mwKu4">electric vehicles</a> have grown significantly and this is expected to continue through the decade.<sup about="#mwt3460" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-926" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-926&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-926" id="mwKu8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKvA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKvE">[</span>926<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKvI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwKvM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-fungible_token" title="Non-fungible token" id="mwKvQ">NFTs</a> as a form of digital art emerged in the 2020s, with NFTs such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everydays:_the_First_5000_Days" title="Everydays: the First 5000 Days" id="mwKvU">Everydays: the First 5000 Days</a>. The NFT market experienced rapid growth during 2020, with its value tripling to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_dollar" title="United States dollar" about="#mwt3461" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwKvY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Currency&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Currency&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;250&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;US&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">US$</a><span about="#mwt3461">250</span> million.<sup about="#mwt3465" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Duffy-2021_927-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Duffy-2021&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Duffy-2021-927&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Duffy-2021-927" id="mwKvc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKvg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKvk">[</span>927<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKvo">]</span></span></a></sup> In the first three months of 2021, more than <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_dollar" title="United States dollar" about="#mwt3462" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwKvs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Currency&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Currency&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;200&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;US&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">US$</a><span about="#mwt3462">200</span> million were spent on NFTs,<sup about="#mwt3468" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Time-2021_928-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Time-2021&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Time-2021-928&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Time-2021-928" id="mwKvw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKv0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKv4">[</span>928<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKv8">]</span></span></a></sup> and in the early months of 2021, interest in NFTs increased after a number of high-profile sales and art auctions.<sup about="#mwt3471" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Howcroft-2021_929-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Howcroft-2021&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Howcroft-2021-929&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Howcroft-2021-929" id="mwKwA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKwE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKwI">[</span>929<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKwM">]</span></span></a></sup> However, by 2022 this market was in the process of rapid collapse.<sup about="#mwt3474" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-930" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-930&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-930" id="mwKwQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKwU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKwY">[</span>930<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKwc">]</span></span></a></sup> A report in September 2023 concluded that 95% of collected NFTs now possess zero market value, and that "79% of all NFT collections remain unsold".<sup about="#mwt3477" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-931" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-931&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-931" id="mwKwg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKwk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKwo">[</span>931<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKws">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="46" id="mwKww" aria-labelledby="Society"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Society">Society</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=46" title="Edit section: Society"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3478" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwKw0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2020s in social history&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt3479" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt3478" id="mwKw4">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020s_in_social_history" title="2020s in social history">2020s in social history</a></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="47" id="mwKw8" aria-labelledby="Social_effects_of_the_COVID-19_pandemic"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Social_effects_of_the_COVID-19_pandemic">Social effects of the COVID-19 pandemic</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=47" title="Edit section: Social effects of the COVID-19 pandemic"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3480" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwKxA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Social impact of the COVID-19 pandemic&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt3481" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt3480" id="mwKxE">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_impact_of_the_COVID-19_pandemic" title="Social impact of the COVID-19 pandemic">Social impact of the COVID-19 pandemic</a></div>

<p id="mwKxI">Medical experts advised, and local authorities often mandated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stay-at-home_order" title="Stay-at-home order" id="mwKxM">stay-at-home orders</a> to prevent gatherings of any size. Such gatherings would be <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impact_of_the_COVID-19_pandemic_on_science_and_technology#Telecommunications" title="Impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on science and technology" id="mwKxQ">replaced by teleconferencing</a>, or in some cases with unconventional attempts to maintain <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_distancing" title="Social distancing" id="mwKxU">social distancing</a> with activities such as a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balcony" title="Balcony" id="mwKxY">balcony</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sing-along" title="Sing-along" id="mwKxc">sing-along</a> for a concert, or a "birthday parade" for a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birthday_party" title="Birthday party" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKxg">birthday party</a>. Replacements for gatherings were seen as significant to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mental_health_during_the_COVID-19_pandemic" title="Mental health during the COVID-19 pandemic" id="mwKxk">mental health during the crisis</a>. Social isolation among <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcohol_drink" title="Alcohol drink" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKxo">alcohol</a> users also adopted a trend towards <i id="mwKxs">Kalsarikänni</i> or "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pantsdrunk" title="Pantsdrunk" id="mwKxw">pantsdrunking</a>", a Finnish antisocial <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drinking_culture" title="Drinking culture" id="mwKx0">drinking culture</a>.</p>

<p id="mwKx4">Low-income individuals were more likely to contract the coronavirus and to die from it. In both New York City and Barcelona, low-income neighborhoods were disproportionately hit by coronavirus cases. Hypotheses for why this was the case included that poorer families were more likely to live in crowded housing and work in jobs deemed essential during the crisis, such as supermarkets and elder care. In the United States, millions of low-income people may lack access to health care due to being <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uninsured" title="Uninsured" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKx8">uninsured</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underinsured" title="Underinsured" id="mwKyA">underinsured</a>. Millions of Americans lost their <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Health_insurance_in_the_United_States" title="Health insurance in the United States" id="mwKyE">health insurance</a> after losing their jobs. Many low-income workers in service jobs became unemployed.</p>

<p id="mwKyI">The coronavirus pandemic was followed by a concern for a potential spike in suicides, exacerbated by social isolation due to quarantine and social-distancing guidelines, fear, and unemployment and financial factors. Many countries reported an increase in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domestic_violence" title="Domestic violence" id="mwKyM">domestic violence</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intimate_partner_violence" title="Intimate partner violence" id="mwKyQ">intimate partner violence</a> attributed to lockdowns amid the COVID-19 pandemic. Financial insecurity, stress, and uncertainty led to increased aggression at home, with abusers able to control large amounts of their victims' daily life. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midlife_crisis" title="Midlife crisis" id="mwKyU">Midlife crisis</a> is a major concern in domestic violence, social implications and suicides for middle-aged adults amid the pandemic. UN Secretary-General <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/António_Guterres" title="António Guterres" id="mwKyY">António Guterres</a> called for a domestic violence and midlife crisis "ceasefire".</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="48" id="mwKyc" aria-labelledby="Population"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Population">Population</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=48" title="Edit section: Population"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwKyg"><li id="mwKyk">The population of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egypt" title="Egypt" id="mwKyo">Egypt</a> reached 100 million in February 2020.<sup about="#mwt3484" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-932" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-932&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-932" id="mwKys"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKyw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKy0">[</span>932<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKy4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwKy8">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_population" title="World population" id="mwKzA">world population</a> reached 8 billion in November 2022.<sup about="#mwt3487" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-933" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-933&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-933" id="mwKzE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKzI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKzM">[</span>933<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKzQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwKzU">Vietnam hit 100 million people in June 2026.<sup about="#mwt3490" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-934" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-934&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-934" id="mwKzY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKzc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKzg">[</span>934<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKzk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwKzo"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Population_growth" title="Population growth" id="mwKzs">Population growth</a>, life expectancy and birth rates declined globally in the early 2020s, driven by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic" title="COVID-19 pandemic" id="mwKzw">COVID-19 pandemic</a>.<sup about="#mwt3493" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-935" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-935&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-935" id="mwKz0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKz4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKz8">[</span>935<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK0A">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwK0E"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India" title="India" id="mwK0I">India</a> surpassed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwK0M">China</a> and became the most-populous country in April 2023.<sup about="#mwt3496" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-936" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-936&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-936" id="mwK0Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK0U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK0Y">[</span>936<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK0c">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="49" id="mwK0g" aria-labelledby="Gender"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Gender">Gender</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=49" title="Edit section: Gender"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3497" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwK0k" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:multiple image&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;\n&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; total_width       = 450\n&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; image1            = Ruotsin pääministeri Magdalena Andersson vieraili Suomessa 5.3.2022 (51919506636).jpg\n&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; caption1          = [[Prime Minister of Sweden|Swedish Prime Minister]] [[Magdalena Andersson]] and [[Prime Minister of Finland|Finnish Prime Minister]] [[Sanna Marin]] were two female prime ministers in [[Scandinavia]] who guided their countries' [[Enlargement of NATO|ascensions]] into [[NATO]].\n&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; image2            = Sanae Takaichi and Giorgia Meloni Italy-Japan summit 08.jpg\n&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; caption2          = [[Prime Minister of Italy|Italian Prime Minister]] [[Giorgia Meloni]] and [[Prime Minister of Japan|Japanese Prime Minister]] [[Sanae Takaichi]] and were two incumbent female prime ministers in Europe and Asia, both became the [[Forbes]]' ''[[Forbes list of the World's 100 Most Powerful Women|World's 100 Most Powerful Women]]''.\n&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1349637415/mw-parser-output/.tmulti" about="#mwt3498" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Multiple image/styles.css&quot;,&quot;wrapper&quot;:&quot;.tmulti&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div class="thumb tmulti floatright" about="#mwt3497"><div class="thumbinner multiimageinner" style="width:442px;max-width:442px"><div class="trow"><div class="tsingle" style="width:219px;max-width:219px"><div class="thumbimage" style="height:144px;overflow:hidden"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Ruotsin_pääministeri_Magdalena_Andersson_vieraili_Suomessa_5.3.2022_(51919506636).jpg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Ruotsin_pääministeri_Magdalena_Andersson_vieraili_Suomessa_5.3.2022_(51919506636).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Ruotsin_p%C3%A4%C3%A4ministeri_Magdalena_Andersson_vieraili_Suomessa_5.3.2022_%2851919506636%29.jpg/250px-Ruotsin_p%C3%A4%C3%A4ministeri_Magdalena_Andersson_vieraili_Suomessa_5.3.2022_%2851919506636%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="3500" data-file-height="2333" data-file-type="bitmap" height="145" width="217" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Ruotsin_p%C3%A4%C3%A4ministeri_Magdalena_Andersson_vieraili_Suomessa_5.3.2022_%2851919506636%29.jpg/500px-Ruotsin_p%C3%A4%C3%A4ministeri_Magdalena_Andersson_vieraili_Suomessa_5.3.2022_%2851919506636%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element"></a></span></div><div class="thumbcaption"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Sweden" title="Prime Minister of Sweden">Swedish Prime Minister</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magdalena_Andersson" title="Magdalena Andersson">Magdalena Andersson</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Finland" title="Prime Minister of Finland">Finnish Prime Minister</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanna_Marin" title="Sanna Marin">Sanna Marin</a> were two female prime ministers in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scandinavia" title="Scandinavia">Scandinavia</a> who guided their countries' <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enlargement_of_NATO" title="Enlargement of NATO">ascensions</a> into <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NATO" title="NATO">NATO</a>.</div></div><div class="tsingle" style="width:219px;max-width:219px"><div class="thumbimage" style="height:144px;overflow:hidden"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sanae_Takaichi_and_Giorgia_Meloni_Italy-Japan_summit_08.jpg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sanae_Takaichi_and_Giorgia_Meloni_Italy-Japan_summit_08.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Sanae_Takaichi_and_Giorgia_Meloni_Italy-Japan_summit_08.jpg/250px-Sanae_Takaichi_and_Giorgia_Meloni_Italy-Japan_summit_08.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2600" data-file-height="1734" data-file-type="bitmap" height="145" width="217" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Sanae_Takaichi_and_Giorgia_Meloni_Italy-Japan_summit_08.jpg/500px-Sanae_Takaichi_and_Giorgia_Meloni_Italy-Japan_summit_08.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element"></a></span></div><div class="thumbcaption"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Italy" title="Prime Minister of Italy">Italian Prime Minister</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giorgia_Meloni" title="Giorgia Meloni">Giorgia Meloni</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Japan" title="Prime Minister of Japan">Japanese Prime Minister</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanae_Takaichi" title="Sanae Takaichi">Sanae Takaichi</a> and were two incumbent female prime ministers in Europe and Asia, both became the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forbes" title="Forbes">Forbes</a>' <i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forbes_list_of_the_World's_100_Most_Powerful_Women" title="Forbes list of the World's 100 Most Powerful Women">World's 100 Most Powerful Women</a></i>.</div></div></div></div></div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3497"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Pages_using_multiple_image_with_auto_scaled_images"></span>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3499" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwK0o" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;See also&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:See_also&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Women in government&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt3500" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt3499" id="mwK0s">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women_in_government" title="Women in government">Women in government</a></div>
<p id="mwK0w">24.3% of all national parliamentarians were women as of February 2019. 11 women were serving as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_elected_and_appointed_female_heads_of_state_and_government" title="List of elected and appointed female heads of state and government" class="mw-redirect" id="mwK00">head of state</a> and 12 as head of government in June 2019. 20.7% of government ministers were women as of January 2019. There are wide regional variations in the average percentages of women parliamentarians. As of February 2019, these were: Nordic countries, 42.5%; Americas, 30.6%; Europe excluding Nordic countries, 27.2%; sub-Saharan Africa, 23.9%; Asia, 19.8%; Arab States, 19%; and the Pacific, 16.3%. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rwanda" title="Rwanda" id="mwK04">Rwanda</a> has the highest number of women parliamentarians worldwide, 61.3% of seats in the lower house. About 26% of elected local parliamentarians are women.<sup about="#mwt3503" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-un_women_937-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;un_women&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-un_women-937&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-un_women-937" id="mwK08"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK1A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK1E">[</span>937<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK1I">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwK1M">Many states swore in their first female leaders during the 2020s, including Presidents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katerina_Sakellaropoulou" title="Katerina Sakellaropoulou" id="mwK1Q">Katerina Sakellaropoulou</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Greece" title="President of Greece" id="mwK1U">Greece</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samia_Suluhu_Hassan" title="Samia Suluhu Hassan" id="mwK1Y">Samia Suluhu Hassan</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Tanzania" title="President of Tanzania" id="mwK1c">Tanzania</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandra_Mason" title="Sandra Mason" id="mwK1g">Sandra Mason</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Barbados" title="President of Barbados" id="mwK1k">Barbados</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xiomara_Castro" title="Xiomara Castro" id="mwK1o">Xiomara Castro</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Honduras" title="President of Honduras" id="mwK1s">Honduras</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katalin_Novák" title="Katalin Novák" id="mwK1w">Katalin Novák</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Hungary" title="President of Hungary" id="mwK10">Hungary</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dina_Boluarte" title="Dina Boluarte" id="mwK14">Dina Boluarte</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Peru" title="President of Peru" id="mwK18">Peru</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nataša_Pirc_Musar" title="Nataša Pirc Musar" id="mwK2A">Nataša Pirc Musar</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Slovenia" title="President of Slovenia" id="mwK2E">Slovenia</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gordana_Siljanovska-Davkova" title="Gordana Siljanovska-Davkova" id="mwK2I">Gordana Siljanovska-Davkova</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_North_Macedonia" title="President of North Macedonia" id="mwK2M">North Macedonia</a>) and Prime Ministers <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_Christiane_Raponda" title="Rose Christiane Raponda" id="mwK2Q">Rose Christiane Raponda</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Gabon" title="Prime Minister of Gabon" id="mwK2U">Gabon</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victoire_Tomegah_Dogbé" title="Victoire Tomegah Dogbé" id="mwK2Y">Victoire Tomegah Dogbé</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_prime_ministers_of_Togo" title="List of prime ministers of Togo" class="mw-redirect" id="mwK2c">Togo</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaja_Kallas" title="Kaja Kallas" id="mwK2g">Kaja Kallas</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Estonia" title="Prime Minister of Estonia" id="mwK2k">Estonia</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiamē_Naomi_Mataʻafa" title="Fiamē Naomi Mataʻafa" id="mwK2o">Fiamē Naomi Mata'afa</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Samoa" title="Prime Minister of Samoa" id="mwK2s">Samoa</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robinah_Nabbanja" title="Robinah Nabbanja" id="mwK2w">Robinah Nabbanja</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Uganda" title="Prime Minister of Uganda" id="mwK20">Uganda</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Najla_Bouden" title="Najla Bouden" id="mwK24">Najla Bouden</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Tunisia" title="Prime Minister of Tunisia" id="mwK28">Tunisia</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magdalena_Andersson" title="Magdalena Andersson" id="mwK3A">Magdalena Andersson</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Sweden" title="Prime Minister of Sweden" id="mwK3E">Sweden</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giorgia_Meloni" title="Giorgia Meloni" id="mwK3I">Giorgia Meloni</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Italy" title="Prime Minister of Italy" id="mwK3M">Italy</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judith_Suminwa" title="Judith Suminwa" id="mwK3Q">Judith Suminwa</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_the_Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo" title="President of the Democratic Republic of the Congo" id="mwK3U">DRC</a>), Chairwoman <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borjana_Krišto" title="Borjana Krišto" id="mwK3Y">Borjana Krišto</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chairman_of_the_Council_of_Ministers_of_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina" title="Chairman of the Council of Ministers of Bosnia and Herzegovina" id="mwK3c">Bosnia and Herzegovina</a>), and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanae_Takaichi" title="Sanae Takaichi" id="mwK3g">Sanae Takaichi</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Japan" title="Prime Minister of Japan" id="mwK3k">Japan</a>).<sup about="#mwt3506" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-938" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-938&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-938" id="mwK3o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK3s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK3w">[</span>938<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK30">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwK34">Despite this, nearly all of the world's wealthiest individuals (mostly <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Tech" title="Big Tech" id="mwK38">American technology</a> billionaires) are male, as are the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_current_heads_of_state_and_government" title="List of current heads of state and government" id="mwK4A">heads of state of most countries</a>.<sup about="#mwt3507" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto_872-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;auto&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-auto-872" id="mwK4E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK4I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK4M">[</span>872<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK4Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="50" id="mwK4U" aria-labelledby="Environmentalism"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Environmentalism">Environmentalism</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=50" title="Edit section: Environmentalism"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3508" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwK4Y" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:multiple image&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;\n&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; total_width       = 450\n&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; image1            = 2011-_Renewable_energy_capacity_-_International_Energy_Agency.svg\n&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; caption1          = [[Renewable energy]] capacity additions in 2020 expanded by more than 45% from 2019, including a 90% rise in global wind capacity and a 23% expansion of new solar photovoltaic installations.<ref name=\&quot;IEA_202306\&quot;>{{#invoke:cite | web |title=Renewable Energy Market Update Outlook for 2023 and 2024 |url=https://iea.blob.core.windows.net/assets/63c14514-6833-4cd8-ac53-f9918c2e4cd9/RenewableEnergyMarketUpdate_June2023.pdf |website=IEA.org |publisher=International Energy Agency (IEA) |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230711115355/https://iea.blob.core.windows.net/assets/63c14514-6833-4cd8-ac53-f9918c2e4cd9/RenewableEnergyMarketUpdate_June2023.pdf |archive-date=11 July 2023 |page=19 |date=June 2023 |quote=IEA. CC BY 4.0. |url-status=live}} ● Source for data through 2016: {{#invoke:cite | web |title=Renewable Energy Market Update / Outlook for 2021 and 2022 |url=https://iea.blob.core.windows.net/assets/18a6041d-bf13-4667-a4c2-8fc008974008/RenewableEnergyMarketUpdate-Outlookfor2021and2022.pdf |website=IEA.org |publisher=International Energy Agency |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230325084025/https://iea.blob.core.windows.net/assets/18a6041d-bf13-4667-a4c2-8fc008974008/RenewableEnergyMarketUpdate-Outlookfor2021and2022.pdf |archive-date=25 March 2023 |page=8 |date=May 2021 |url-status=live |quote=IEA. Licence: CC BY 4.0 }}</ref>\n&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; image2            = 1940-2024 Global surface temperature - stacked - Copernicus.jpg\n&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; caption2          = In 2024, Earth saw the highest average annual surface air temperature ever recorded, outpacing 2023 on an average basis.<ref name=\&quot;CopernicusGMST_thru2024\&quot;>{{#invoke:cite | web |date=15 January 2025 |title=The 2024 Annual Climate Summary / Global Climate Highlights 2024 |url=https://sites.ecmwf.int/data/c3sci/global-climate-highlights/2024/chart-gallery/supplementary/GCH2024-gallery-figureS1/figureS1.pdf |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250115224213/https://sites.ecmwf.int/data/c3sci/global-climate-highlights/2024/chart-gallery/supplementary/GCH2024-gallery-figureS1/figureS1.pdf |archive-date=15 January 2025 |publisher=Copernicus Programme}}</ref>\n&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1349637415/mw-parser-output/.tmulti" about="#mwt3509" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Multiple image/styles.css&quot;,&quot;wrapper&quot;:&quot;.tmulti&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div class="thumb tmulti floatright" about="#mwt3508"><div class="thumbinner multiimageinner" style="width:442px;max-width:442px"><div class="trow"><div class="tsingle" style="width:251px;max-width:251px"><div class="thumbimage" style="height:140px;overflow:hidden"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2011-_Renewable_energy_capacity_-_International_Energy_Agency.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2011-_Renewable_energy_capacity_-_International_Energy_Agency.svg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/2011-_Renewable_energy_capacity_-_International_Energy_Agency.svg/250px-2011-_Renewable_energy_capacity_-_International_Energy_Agency.svg.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="675" data-file-type="drawing" height="140" width="249" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/2011-_Renewable_energy_capacity_-_International_Energy_Agency.svg/500px-2011-_Renewable_energy_capacity_-_International_Energy_Agency.svg.png 2x" class="mw-file-element"></a></span></div><div class="thumbcaption"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renewable_energy" title="Renewable energy">Renewable energy</a> capacity additions in 2020 expanded by more than 45% from 2019, including a 90% rise in global wind capacity and a 23% expansion of new solar photovoltaic installations.<sup about="#mwt3514" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-IEA_202306_939-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;IEA_202306&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-IEA_202306-939&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-IEA_202306-939" id="mwK4c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK4g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK4k">[</span>939<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK4o">]</span></span></a></sup></div></div><div class="tsingle" style="width:187px;max-width:187px"><div class="thumbimage" style="height:140px;overflow:hidden"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:1940-2024_Global_surface_temperature_-_stacked_-_Copernicus.jpg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:1940-2024_Global_surface_temperature_-_stacked_-_Copernicus.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/1940-2024_Global_surface_temperature_-_stacked_-_Copernicus.jpg/250px-1940-2024_Global_surface_temperature_-_stacked_-_Copernicus.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2774" data-file-height="2108" data-file-type="bitmap" height="141" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/1940-2024_Global_surface_temperature_-_stacked_-_Copernicus.jpg/500px-1940-2024_Global_surface_temperature_-_stacked_-_Copernicus.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element"></a></span></div><div class="thumbcaption">In 2024, Earth saw the highest average annual surface air temperature ever recorded, outpacing 2023 on an average basis.<sup about="#mwt3520" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CopernicusGMST_thru2024_940-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;CopernicusGMST_thru2024&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-CopernicusGMST_thru2024-940&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-CopernicusGMST_thru2024-940" id="mwK4s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK4w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK40">[</span>940<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK44">]</span></span></a></sup></div></div></div></div></div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3508"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Pages_using_multiple_image_with_auto_scaled_images"></span>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3523" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwK48" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;See also&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:See_also&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2020s in environmental history&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt3524" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt3523" id="mwK5A">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020s_in_environmental_history" title="2020s in environmental history">2020s in environmental history</a></div>
<p id="mwK5E">The effects of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_change" title="Climate change" id="mwK5I">climate change</a> manifested in 2020 with a record 30 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atlantic_hurricane" title="Atlantic hurricane" id="mwK5M">named Atlantic tropical storms and hurricanes</a>; the highest heat in 80-years recorded at 54.4 Celsius; massive wildfires <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019–20_Australian_bushfire_season" title="2019–20 Australian bushfire season" id="mwK5Q">in Australia</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Western_United_States_wildfire_season" title="2020 Western United States wildfire season" id="mwK5U">Western United States</a>, and the Arctic; and the second-lowest annual <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic_sea_ice_decline" title="Arctic sea ice decline" id="mwK5Y">Arctic sea ice coverage</a>.<sup about="#mwt3527" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-941" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-941&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-941" id="mwK5c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK5g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK5k">[</span>941<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK5o">]</span></span></a></sup> The Net Zero Asset Managers initiative—involving 30 fund management companies managing $9 trillion—pledged investment portfolios to be <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_neutrality" title="Carbon neutrality" class="mw-redirect" id="mwK5s">carbon-neutral</a> by 2050.<sup about="#mwt3530" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Bloomberg_20201216_942-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Bloomberg_20201216&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bloomberg_20201216-942&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Bloomberg_20201216-942" id="mwK5w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK50"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK54">[</span>942<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK58">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwK6A">In July 2024, in each month in a 12-month period (through June 2024), Earth's average temperature exceeded 1.5<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwK6E">&nbsp;</span>°C above the pre-industrial baseline,<sup about="#mwt3535" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-InsideClimateNews_20240709_943-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;InsideClimateNews_20240709&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-InsideClimateNews_20240709-943&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-InsideClimateNews_20240709-943" id="mwK6I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK6M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK6Q">[</span>943<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK6U">]</span></span></a></sup> and the highest daily global average temperature is recorded at <span about="#mwt3531" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwK6Y" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Convert&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Convert&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;17.09&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;C&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;F&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">17.09</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt3531">&nbsp;</span><span about="#mwt3531">°C (62.76</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt3531">&nbsp;</span><span about="#mwt3531">°F)</span>, surpassing the previous record of <span about="#mwt3532" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwK6c" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Convert&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Convert&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;17.08&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;C&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;F&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">17.08</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt3532">&nbsp;</span><span about="#mwt3532">°C (62.74</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt3532">&nbsp;</span><span about="#mwt3532">°F)</span> on 6 July 2023.<sup about="#mwt3538" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-944" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-944&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-944" id="mwK6g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK6k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK6o">[</span>944<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK6s">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<ul id="mwK6w"><li id="mwK60"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Team_Seas" title="Team Seas" id="mwK64">Team Seas</a> is an international collaborative fundraiser founded by YouTubers <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Rober" title="Mark Rober" id="mwK68">Mark Rober</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MrBeast" title="MrBeast" id="mwK7A">MrBeast</a> on 29 October 2021, as a follow-up to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Team_Trees" title="Team Trees" id="mwK7E">Team Trees</a>. The fundraiser's aim was to raise US$30 million to remove 30 million pounds of trash from the ocean by the end of the year. They also partnered with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ocean_Cleanup" title="Ocean Cleanup" class="mw-redirect" id="mwK7I">Ocean Cleanup</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ocean_Conservancy" title="Ocean Conservancy" id="mwK7M">Ocean Conservancy</a>.</li>
<li id="mwK7Q">Members of the United Nations agree on a legal framework for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Seas_Treaty" title="High Seas Treaty" id="mwK7U">High Seas Treaty</a> on 4 March 2023, which aims to protect 30% of the world's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ocean" title="Ocean" id="mwK7Y">oceans</a> by 2030.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="51" id="mwK7c" aria-labelledby="LGBTQ_rights"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="LGBTQ_rights">LGBTQ rights</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=51" title="Edit section: LGBTQ rights"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwK7g"><li id="mwK7k">A law allowing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_gender" title="Third gender" id="mwK7o">third gender</a> option on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Driver_licenses" title="Driver licenses" class="mw-redirect" id="mwK7s">driver licenses</a> took effect in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_rights_in_New_Hampshire" title="LGBTQ rights in New Hampshire" id="mwK7w">New Hampshire</a>.<sup about="#mwt3541" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-945" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-945&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-945" id="mwK70"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK74"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK78">[</span>945<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK8A">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwK8E"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_rights_in_Switzerland" title="LGBTQ rights in Switzerland" id="mwK8I">Switzerland</a> banned discrimination based on sexuality due to a referendum, putting into effect a law previously introduced in 2018, that was subsequently blocked by the government that requested a referendum to be held on the matter first.<sup about="#mwt3544" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-946" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-946&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-946" id="mwK8M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK8Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK8U">[</span>946<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK8Y">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwK8c">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_rights_in_Northern_Ireland" title="LGBTQ rights in Northern Ireland" id="mwK8g">Northern Ireland</a>, the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Same-sex_marriage" title="Same-sex marriage" id="mwK8k">same-sex marriage</a> took place after legalizing legislation took effect in January 2020.<sup about="#mwt3547" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-947" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-947&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-947" id="mwK8o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK8s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK8w">[</span>947<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK80">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3550" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-948" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-948&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-948" id="mwK84"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK88"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK9A">[</span>948<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK9E">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<!--&#x2D;===Youth culture===-->
<li id="mwK9I">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_rights_in_Costa_Rica" title="LGBTQ rights in Costa Rica" id="mwK9M">Costa Rica</a>, same-sex marriage and joint adoption by same-sex couples became legal on 26 May 2020.</li>
<li id="mwK9Q">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_the_United_States" title="Supreme Court of the United States" id="mwK9U">Supreme Court of the United States</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bostock_v._Clayton_County" title="Bostock v. Clayton County" id="mwK9Y">ruled</a> that job discrimination against workers for their <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sexual_orientation" title="Sexual orientation" id="mwK9c">sexual orientation</a> or gender identity is illegal.<sup about="#mwt3553" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-949" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-949&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-949" id="mwK9g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK9k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK9o">[</span>949<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK9s">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwK9w">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_rights_in_Argentina" title="LGBTQ rights in Argentina" id="mwK90">Argentina</a>, nonbinary <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ID_card" title="ID card" class="mw-redirect" id="mwK94">ID cards</a> with an "X" gender marker started to be issued by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_the_Interior_(Argentina)" title="Ministry of the Interior (Argentina)" id="mwK98">Ministry of the Interior</a>.</li>
<li id="mwK-A">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Department_of_State" title="United States Department of State" id="mwK-E">U.S State Department</a> issued its first ever passport with an "X" gender marker in October 2021, intended to support nonbinary people.<sup about="#mwt3556" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-950" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-950&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-950" id="mwK-I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK-M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK-Q">[</span>950<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK-U">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwK-Y">Same-sex marriage became <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_rights_in_Switzerland" title="LGBTQ rights in Switzerland" id="mwK-c">legal</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Switzerland" title="Switzerland" id="mwK-g">Switzerland</a> after a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_Swiss_same-sex_marriage_referendum" title="2021 Swiss same-sex marriage referendum" id="mwK-k">2021 referendum</a>, enforced beginning in July 2022.</li>
<li id="mwK-o">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_rights_in_Chile" title="LGBTQ rights in Chile" id="mwK-s">Chile</a>, same-sex marriage and joint adoption by same-sex couples became legal on 10 March 2022.</li>
<li id="mwK-w">Same-sex marriage became <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_rights_in_Slovenia" title="LGBTQ rights in Slovenia" id="mwK-0">legal</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slovenia" title="Slovenia" id="mwK-4">Slovenia</a> on 8 July 2022 after the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitutional_Court_of_Slovenia" title="Constitutional Court of Slovenia" id="mwK-8">Constitutional Court of Slovenia</a> ruled that the ban on same-sex marriages violated the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Slovenia" title="Constitution of Slovenia" id="mwK_A">national constitution</a>.</li>
<li id="mwK_E">Same-sex marriage became <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_rights_in_Cuba" title="LGBTQ rights in Cuba" id="mwK_I">legal</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba" title="Cuba" id="mwK_M">Cuba</a> on 27 September 2022 after the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Cuban_Family_Code_referendum" title="2022 Cuban Family Code referendum" id="mwK_Q">Cuban Family Code referendum</a> passed.</li>
<li id="mwK_U">By October 2022, Mexico City and all Mexican states had <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Same-sex_marriage_in_Mexico" title="Same-sex marriage in Mexico" id="mwK_Y">legalized same-sex marriage</a>, either by legislation, executive action, or Supreme Court order.<sup about="#mwt3559" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-951" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-951&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-951" id="mwK_c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwK_g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK_k">[</span>951<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwK_o">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwK_s">On 1 January 2024, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Same-sex_marriage_in_Estonia" title="Same-sex marriage in Estonia" id="mwK_w">same-sex marriage</a> became legal in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Estonia" title="Estonia" id="mwK_0">Estonia</a>.</li></ul>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="52" id="mwK_4" aria-labelledby="Global_goals_and_issues"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Global_goals_and_issues">Global goals and issues</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=52" title="Edit section: Global goals and issues"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwK_8">Development in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_global_issues" title="List of global issues" id="mwLAA">global goals and issues</a>—including goals or progress related to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_causes_of_death_by_rate" title="List of causes of death by rate" id="mwLAE">largest causes of human death</a>—during the decade, according to reports that systematically track, quantify or review associated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Progress" title="Progress" id="mwLAI">progress</a>.</p>

<p id="mwLAM"><b id="mwLAQ">As of 2022:</b></p>
<ul id="mwLAU"><li id="mwLAY">Progress of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Agreement" title="Paris Agreement" id="mwLAc">Paris Agreement</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_issue" title="Global issue" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLAg">global</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_change_mitigation" title="Climate change mitigation" id="mwLAk">climate change mitigation</a> goals
<ul id="mwLAo"><li id="mwLAs">The United in Science 2022 report by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Meteorological_Organization" title="World Meteorological Organization" id="mwLAw">WMO</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Executive_summary" title="Executive summary" id="mwLA0">summarizes</a> latest climate science-related updates and assesses recent <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_change_mitigation" title="Climate change mitigation" id="mwLA4">climate change mitigation</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Progress" title="Progress" id="mwLA8">progress</a> as "going in the wrong direction".<sup about="#mwt3562" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-952" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-952&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-952" id="mwLBA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLBE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLBI">[</span>952<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLBM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3565" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-953" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-953&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-953" id="mwLBQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLBU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLBY">[</span>953<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLBc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwLBg">A report by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Resources_Institute" title="World Resources Institute" id="mwLBk">World Resources Institute</a> assesses the state of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nationally_determined_contributions" title="Nationally determined contributions" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLBo">nationally determined contributions</a> (NDCs), finding they need to be strengthened by about six times for alignment with what may be enough to reach the Paris Agreement's 1.5<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwLBs">&nbsp;</span>°C goal.<sup about="#mwt3568" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-954" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-954&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-954" id="mwLBw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLB0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLB4">[</span>954<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLB8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3571" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-955" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-955&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-955" id="mwLCA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLCE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLCI">[</span>955<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLCM">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UNFCCC" title="UNFCCC" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLCQ">UNFCCC</a>'s NDC synthesis report suggests that based on the latest NDCs the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_budget" title="Carbon budget" id="mwLCU">carbon budget</a> for a 50% likelihood of limiting warming to 1.5<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwLCY">&nbsp;</span>°C would be used up by around 2032.<sup about="#mwt3572" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nytpledges_956-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;nytpledges&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-nytpledges-956" id="mwLCc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLCg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLCk">[</span>956<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLCo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3575" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-957" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-957&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-957" id="mwLCs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLCw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLC0">[</span>957<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLC4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3578" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cop27_958-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;cop27&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-cop27-958&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-cop27-958" id="mwLC8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLDA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLDE">[</span>958<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLDI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3583" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-959" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-959&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-959" id="mwLDM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLDQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLDU">[</span>959<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLDY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwLDc">A <i id="mwLDg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lancet" title="The Lancet" id="mwLDk">Lancet</a> Countdown</i> report publishes data of indicators that show "countries and companies continue to make choices that threaten the health and survival of people in every part of the world". It calls for an immediate, health-centred response at a critical juncture of recovery from crises.<sup about="#mwt3586" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nytpledges_956-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;nytpledges&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-nytpledges-956&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-nytpledges-956" id="mwLDo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLDs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLDw">[</span>956<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLD0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3589" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-960" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-960&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-960" id="mwLD4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLD8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLEA">[</span>960<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLEE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwLEI">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WMO" title="WMO" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLEM">WMO</a> reports atmospheric levels of the three main <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenhouse_gas" title="Greenhouse gas" id="mwLEQ">greenhouse gases</a>, carbon dioxide, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methane_emissions" title="Methane emissions" id="mwLEU">methane</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nitrous_oxide" title="Nitrous oxide" id="mwLEY">nitrous oxide</a>, all reached record highs, with methane concentrations showing a record jump in 2021. The WMO Secretary-General concludes that "we are heading in the wrong direction", with time "running out".<sup about="#mwt3592" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-961" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-961&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-961" id="mwLEc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLEg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLEk">[</span>961<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLEo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3595" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-962" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-962&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-962" id="mwLEs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLEw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLE0">[</span>962<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLE4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwLE8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_Action_Tracker" title="Climate Action Tracker" id="mwLFA">Climate Action Tracker</a> systematically <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_change_mitigation#Monitoring" title="Climate change mitigation" id="mwLFE">assesses the state of progress of actions of climate goals</a> in an overview, finding that none of the indicators is on track to reach their 2030 targets, with insufficient speed for six indicators, and well below the required pace for 21, five heading in the wrong direction, and data being insufficient to evaluate the remaining eight.<sup about="#mwt3598" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-963" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-963&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-963" id="mwLFI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLFM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLFQ">[</span>963<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLFU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3601" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-964" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-964&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-964" id="mwLFY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLFc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLFg">[</span>964<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLFk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3604" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-965" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-965&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-965" id="mwLFo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLFs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLFw">[</span>965<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLF0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwLF4">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UNEP" title="UNEP" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLF8">UNEP</a>'s Emissions Gap Report finds that no credible "pathway" to the 1.5<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwLGA">&nbsp;</span>°C climate goal is in place.<sup about="#mwt3607" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-966" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-966&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-966" id="mwLGE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLGI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLGM">[</span>966<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLGQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3610" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-967" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-967&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-967" id="mwLGU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLGY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLGc">[</span>967<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLGg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3613" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-968" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-968&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-968" id="mwLGk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLGo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLGs">[</span>968<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLGw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3616" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-969" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-969&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-969" id="mwLG0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLG4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLG8">[</span>969<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLHA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3619" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-970" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-970&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-970" id="mwLHE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLHI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLHM">[</span>970<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLHQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Similarly, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UNFCCC" title="UNFCCC" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLHU">UNFCCC</a> synthesis about "long-term low-emission development strategies" warns that many net-zero targets "remain uncertain and postpone into the future critical action that needs to take place now".<sup about="#mwt3622" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-971" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-971&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-971" id="mwLHY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLHc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLHg">[</span>971<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLHk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3625" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-972" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-972&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-972" id="mwLHo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLHs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLHw">[</span>972<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLH0">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwLH4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deforestation" title="Deforestation" id="mwLH8">Deforestation</a> mitigation goals
<ul id="mwLIA"><li id="mwLIE">An annual report by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Resources_Institute" title="World Resources Institute" id="mwLII">World Resources Institute</a> shows that tropical regions lost 9.3 million acres of primary old-growth forest in 2021, a decline of 11% from 2020, and about equal to both 2018 and 2019.<sup about="#mwt3628" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-973" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-973&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-973" id="mwLIM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLIQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLIU">[</span>973<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLIY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3631" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-974" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-974&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-974" id="mwLIc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLIg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLIk">[</span>974<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLIo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwLIs">The Forest Declaration Assessment finds that a drop of only 6.3% in deforestation in 2021 is "leaving the world off track from its goals of ending forest loss by 2030".<sup about="#mwt3634" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-975" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-975&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-975" id="mwLIw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLI0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLI4">[</span>975<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLI8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3637" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-976" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-976&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-976" id="mwLJA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLJE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLJI">[</span>976<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLJM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3640" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-977" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-977&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-977" id="mwLJQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLJU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLJY">[</span>977<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLJc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3643" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-978" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-978&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-978" id="mwLJg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLJk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLJo">[</span>978<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLJs">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwLJw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_health" title="Public health" id="mwLJ0">Public health</a> goals
<ul id="mwLJ4"><li id="mwLJ8">The UN's "The State of Food Security and Nutrition in the World" report finds that the number of people affected by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunger" title="Hunger" id="mwLKA">hunger</a> globally rose by 46 million to 828 million in 2021. 3.1 billion people could not afford a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Healthy_diet" title="Healthy diet" id="mwLKE">healthy diet</a> in 2020, an increase of 112 million from 2019.<sup about="#mwt3646" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-979" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-979&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-979" id="mwLKI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLKM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLKQ">[</span>979<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLKU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3649" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-980" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-980&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-980" id="mwLKY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLKc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLKg">[</span>980<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLKk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwLKo">A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WHO" title="WHO" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLKs">WHO</a> report indicates collective progress toward a 15% relative reduction in population levels of physical inactivity by 2030 is insufficient and that about 500 million people will develop <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart_disease" title="Heart disease" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLKw">heart disease</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Obesity" title="Obesity" id="mwLK0">obesity</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diabetes" title="Diabetes" id="mwLK4">diabetes</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-communicable_disease#Global_health" title="Non-communicable disease" id="mwLK8">other diseases</a> if they do not increase their <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physical_activity" title="Physical activity" id="mwLLA">physical activity</a>.<sup about="#mwt3652" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-981" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-981&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-981" id="mwLLE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLLI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLLM">[</span>981<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLLQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3655" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-982" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-982&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-982" id="mwLLU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLLY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLLc">[</span>982<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLLg">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwLLk">Global <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Budget" title="Budget" id="mwLLo">budgets</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_spending" title="Government spending" id="mwLLs">government spending</a>
<ul id="mwLLw"><li id="mwLL0">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OECD" title="OECD" id="mwLL4">OECD</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Energy_Agency" title="International Energy Agency" id="mwLL8">IEA</a> report that global public <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fossil_fuel_subsidies" title="Fossil fuel subsidies" id="mwLMA">subsidies for fossil fuels</a> almost doubled from 2020 to $700bn in 2021.<sup about="#mwt3658" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-983" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-983&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-983" id="mwLME"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLMI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLMM">[</span>983<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLMQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3661" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-984" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-984&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-984" id="mwLMU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLMY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLMc">[</span>984<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLMg">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwLMk">General <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Well-being" title="Well-being" id="mwLMo">well-being</a>
<ul id="mwLMs"><li id="mwLMw">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Club_of_Rome" title="Club of Rome" id="mwLM0">Club of Rome</a>, authors of the 1972 <i id="mwLM4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Limits_to_Growth" title="The Limits to Growth" id="mwLM8">The Limits to Growth</a></i>, and research institutes like the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potsdam_Institute_for_Climate_Impact_Research" title="Potsdam Institute for Climate Impact Research" id="mwLNA">Potsdam Institute for Climate Impact Research</a> publish the "Earth for All" report, concluding that to increase the wellbeing of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humankind" title="Humankind" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLNE">humanity</a>, addressing rising inequality is key to mitigating related issues such as climate change with many current <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Policy" title="Policy" id="mwLNI">policies</a> disproportionately burdening lower income groups.<sup about="#mwt3664" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-985" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-985&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-985" id="mwLNM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLNQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLNU">[</span>985<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLNY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3667" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-986" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-986&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-986" id="mwLNc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLNk">[</span>986<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLNo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3670" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-987" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-987&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-987" id="mwLNs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLNw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLN0">[</span>987<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLN4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3673" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-COR_2022_988-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;COR_2022&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-COR_2022-988&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-COR_2022-988" id="mwLN8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLOA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLOE">[</span>988<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLOI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3677" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-EFA_2022_989-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;EFA_2022&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-EFA_2022-989&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-EFA_2022-989" id="mwLOM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLOQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLOU">[</span>989<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLOY">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwLOc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sustainable_Development_Goals" title="Sustainable Development Goals" id="mwLOg">Sustainable Development Goals</a> (other than the above or in general)
<ul id="mwLOk"><li id="mwLOo">The only UN report that monitors global progress on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2030_Agenda_for_Sustainable_Development" title="2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLOs">2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development</a> indicates the agenda is in "grave danger".<sup about="#mwt3680" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-990" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-990&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-990" id="mwLOw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLO0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLO4">[</span>990<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLO8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3683" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-991" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-991&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-991" id="mwLPA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLPE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLPI">[</span>991<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLPM">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwLPQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gross_domestic_product" title="Gross domestic product" id="mwLPU">GDP</a>-alternative <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Progress" title="Progress" id="mwLPY">progress</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sustainable_development" title="Sustainable development" id="mwLPc">sustainable development</a> indices
<ul id="mwLPg"><li id="mwLPk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_Development_Index" title="Human Development Index" id="mwLPo">Human Development Index</a> (HDI): the Human Development Report 2021–22 concludes that for the first time, the global HDI value declined for a second year, with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Living_standard" title="Living standard" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLPs">living standards</a> declining in 90% of countries.<sup about="#mwt3686" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-992" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-992&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-992" id="mwLPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLP0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLP4">[</span>992<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLP8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3689" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-993" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-993&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-993" id="mwLQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLQE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQI">[</span>993<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3692" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-994" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-994&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-994" id="mwLQQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLQU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQY">[</span>994<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQc">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="53" id="mwLQg" aria-labelledby="Popular_culture"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Popular_culture">Popular culture</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=53" title="Edit section: Popular culture"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul class="gallery mw-gallery-traditional left" style="max-width: 912px;" typeof="mw:Extension/gallery" about="#mwt3693" id="mwLQk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;gallery&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;class&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;widths&quot;:&quot;185&quot;,&quot;heights&quot;:&quot;140&quot;,&quot;perrow&quot;:&quot;4&quot;,&quot;align&quot;:&quot;left&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{}}">
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLQo"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLQs"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLQw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:PS5Digitalprerefined.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="The ninth generation of video game consoles, like PlayStation 5 (pictured) and Xbox Series X, were both released in 2020. Games for PlayStation 5 such as FC 24, The Matrix Awakens, and Overwatch 2 used HyperMotion and Unreal Engine 5 to display more realistic graphics. Grand Theft Auto VI is planned for release on ninth-generation consoles in 2026." id="mwLQ0"><img alt="The ninth generation of video game consoles, like PlayStation 5 (pictured) and Xbox Series X, were both released in 2020. Games for PlayStation 5 such as FC 24, The Matrix Awakens, and Overwatch 2 used HyperMotion and Unreal Engine 5 to display more realistic graphics. Grand Theft Auto VI is planned for release on ninth-generation consoles in 2026." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:PS5Digitalprerefined.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/PS5Digitalprerefined.jpg/120px-PS5Digitalprerefined.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="1229" data-file-height="2048" data-file-type="bitmap" height="140" width="84" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/PS5Digitalprerefined.jpg/250px-PS5Digitalprerefined.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLQ4"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLQ8">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninth_generation_of_video_game_consoles" title="Ninth generation of video game consoles" id="mwLRA">ninth generation of video game consoles</a>, like <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PlayStation_5" title="PlayStation 5" id="mwLRE">PlayStation 5</a> (pictured) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xbox_Series_X" title="Xbox Series X" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLRI">Xbox Series X</a>, were both released in 2020. Games for PlayStation 5 such as <i id="mwLRM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EA_Sports_FC_24" title="EA Sports FC 24" id="mwLRQ">FC 24</a></i>, <i id="mwLRU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Matrix_Awakens" title="The Matrix Awakens" id="mwLRY">The Matrix Awakens</a></i>, and <i id="mwLRc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overwatch_2" title="Overwatch 2" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLRg">Overwatch 2</a></i> used HyperMotion and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unreal_Engine_5" title="Unreal Engine 5" id="mwLRk">Unreal Engine 5</a> to display more realistic graphics. <i id="mwLRo"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Theft_Auto_VI" title="Grand Theft Auto VI" id="mwLRs">Grand Theft Auto VI</a></i> is planned for release on ninth-generation consoles in 2026.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLRw"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLR0"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLR4"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:TikTok_exhibition_stand_at_Gamescom_2022_in_Cologne,_Germany_(52760217055).jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="The video-sharing site TikTok became a major influence on pop culture and the music industry in the early 2020s. Short-form videos have increased in viewership through Instagram Reels, Facebook Reels and YouTube Shorts during the decade." id="mwLR8"><img alt="The video-sharing site TikTok became a major influence on pop culture and the music industry in the early 2020s. Short-form videos have increased in viewership through Instagram Reels, Facebook Reels and YouTube Shorts during the decade." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:TikTok_exhibition_stand_at_Gamescom_2022_in_Cologne,_Germany_(52760217055).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/TikTok_exhibition_stand_at_Gamescom_2022_in_Cologne%2C_Germany_%2852760217055%29.jpg/250px-TikTok_exhibition_stand_at_Gamescom_2022_in_Cologne%2C_Germany_%2852760217055%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="6240" data-file-height="4160" data-file-type="bitmap" height="123" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/TikTok_exhibition_stand_at_Gamescom_2022_in_Cologne%2C_Germany_%2852760217055%29.jpg/500px-TikTok_exhibition_stand_at_Gamescom_2022_in_Cologne%2C_Germany_%2852760217055%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLSA"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLSE">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Video-sharing" title="Video-sharing" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLSI">video-sharing</a> site <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TikTok" title="TikTok" id="mwLSM">TikTok</a> became a major influence on pop culture and the music industry in the early 2020s. Short-form videos have increased in viewership through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instagram#Reels" title="Instagram" id="mwLSQ">Instagram Reels</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facebook_Reels" title="Facebook Reels" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLSU">Facebook Reels</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube_Shorts" title="YouTube Shorts" id="mwLSY">YouTube Shorts</a> during the decade.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLSc"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLSg"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLSk"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:101_Albright_Way.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="The streaming wars got bigger in the 2020s as many new streaming services such as Disney+, Apple TV+, HBO Max, and Paramount+ competed against Netflix, Hulu, and Amazon Prime Video." id="mwLSo"><img alt="The streaming wars got bigger in the 2020s as many new streaming services such as Disney+, Apple TV+, HBO Max, and Paramount+ competed against Netflix, Hulu, and Amazon Prime Video." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:101_Albright_Way.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/101_Albright_Way.jpg/250px-101_Albright_Way.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="5024" data-file-height="3188" data-file-type="bitmap" height="117" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/101_Albright_Way.jpg/500px-101_Albright_Way.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLSs"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLSw">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Streaming_media#Streaming_wars" title="Streaming media" id="mwLS0">streaming wars</a> got bigger in the 2020s as many new streaming services such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disney+" title="Disney+" id="mwLS4">Disney+</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_TV+" title="Apple TV+" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLS8">Apple TV+</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HBO_Max" title="HBO Max" id="mwLTA">HBO Max</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paramount+" title="Paramount+" id="mwLTE">Paramount+</a> competed against <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netflix" title="Netflix" id="mwLTI">Netflix</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hulu" title="Hulu" id="mwLTM">Hulu</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Prime_Video" title="Amazon Prime Video" id="mwLTQ">Amazon Prime Video</a>.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLTU"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLTY"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLTc"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Karine_Jean-Pierre_is_joined_by_the_cast_of_Ted_Lasso_for_a_press_briefing_(52834074267).jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="The decade saw popularized TV shows of the decade such as Ted Lasso (the cast being pictured above), Squid Game, The Boys, The Mandalorian, Wednesday, Peacemaker, Shōgun, Severance, Euphoria, Abbott Elementary, Nobody Wants This, and Only Murders in the Building." id="mwLTg"><img alt="The decade saw popularized TV shows of the decade such as Ted Lasso (the cast being pictured above), Squid Game, The Boys, The Mandalorian, Wednesday, Peacemaker, Shōgun, Severance, Euphoria, Abbott Elementary, Nobody Wants This, and Only Murders in the Building." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Karine_Jean-Pierre_is_joined_by_the_cast_of_Ted_Lasso_for_a_press_briefing_(52834074267).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Karine_Jean-Pierre_is_joined_by_the_cast_of_Ted_Lasso_for_a_press_briefing_%2852834074267%29.jpg/250px-Karine_Jean-Pierre_is_joined_by_the_cast_of_Ted_Lasso_for_a_press_briefing_%2852834074267%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="6770" data-file-height="4513" data-file-type="bitmap" height="123" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Karine_Jean-Pierre_is_joined_by_the_cast_of_Ted_Lasso_for_a_press_briefing_%2852834074267%29.jpg/500px-Karine_Jean-Pierre_is_joined_by_the_cast_of_Ted_Lasso_for_a_press_briefing_%2852834074267%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLTk"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLTo">The decade saw popularized TV shows of the decade such as <i id="mwLTs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ted_Lasso" title="Ted Lasso" id="mwLTw">Ted Lasso</a></i> (the cast being pictured above), <i id="mwLT0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squid_Game" title="Squid Game" id="mwLT4">Squid Game</a></i>, <i id="mwLT8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Boys_(TV_series)" title="The Boys (TV series)" id="mwLUA">The Boys</a></i>, <i id="mwLUE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mandalorian" title="The Mandalorian" id="mwLUI">The Mandalorian</a></i>, <i id="mwLUM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wednesday_(TV_series)" title="Wednesday (TV series)" id="mwLUQ">Wednesday</a></i>, <i id="mwLUU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peacemaker_(TV_series)" title="Peacemaker (TV series)" id="mwLUY">Peacemaker</a></i>, <i id="mwLUc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shōgun_(2024_TV_series)" title="Shōgun (2024 TV series)" id="mwLUg">Shōgun</a></i>, <i id="mwLUk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Severance_(TV_series)" title="Severance (TV series)" id="mwLUo">Severance</a></i>, <i id="mwLUs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euphoria_(American_TV_series)" title="Euphoria (American TV series)" id="mwLUw">Euphoria</a></i>, <i id="mwLU0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbott_Elementary" title="Abbott Elementary" id="mwLU4">Abbott Elementary</a></i>, <i id="mwLU8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nobody_Wants_This" title="Nobody Wants This" id="mwLVA">Nobody Wants This</a></i>, and <i id="mwLVE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Only_Murders_in_the_Building" title="Only Murders in the Building" id="mwLVI">Only Murders in the Building</a></i>.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLVM"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLVQ"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLVU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Airpods_and_Airpods_Pro_being_displayed_in_electronics_retail_store.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="AirPods have dominated the wireless headphone market in the early 2020s. Pictured are the base and &quot;Pro&quot; model of AirPods respectively. AirPods allow users to be several feet away from their device via Bluetooth, a technology not seen in wired earbuds of previous decades." id="mwLVY"><img alt="AirPods have dominated the wireless headphone market in the early 2020s. Pictured are the base and &quot;Pro&quot; model of AirPods respectively. AirPods allow users to be several feet away from their device via Bluetooth, a technology not seen in wired earbuds of previous decades." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Airpods_and_Airpods_Pro_being_displayed_in_electronics_retail_store.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Airpods_and_Airpods_Pro_being_displayed_in_electronics_retail_store.jpg/250px-Airpods_and_Airpods_Pro_being_displayed_in_electronics_retail_store.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="3061" data-file-height="2061" data-file-type="bitmap" height="125" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Airpods_and_Airpods_Pro_being_displayed_in_electronics_retail_store.jpg/500px-Airpods_and_Airpods_Pro_being_displayed_in_electronics_retail_store.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLVc"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLVg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AirPods" title="AirPods" id="mwLVk">AirPods</a> have dominated the wireless headphone market in the early 2020s. Pictured are the base and "Pro" model of AirPods respectively. AirPods allow users to be several feet away from their device via <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluetooth" title="Bluetooth" id="mwLVo">Bluetooth</a>, a technology not seen in wired earbuds of previous decades.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLVs"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLVw"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLV0"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ALTer_EGO_1_18_2020_(50740816801).jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Flashy multi-colored clothing became a trend in the early 2020s, as did baggier clothing such as hoodies, modelled here by musician Billie Eilish. The 2020s revived and built upon Y2K fashion trends." id="mwLV4"><img alt="Flashy multi-colored clothing became a trend in the early 2020s, as did baggier clothing such as hoodies, modelled here by musician Billie Eilish. The 2020s revived and built upon Y2K fashion trends." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ALTer_EGO_1_18_2020_(50740816801).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/ALTer_EGO_1_18_2020_%2850740816801%29.jpg/120px-ALTer_EGO_1_18_2020_%2850740816801%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2000" data-file-height="2800" data-file-type="bitmap" height="140" width="100" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/ALTer_EGO_1_18_2020_%2850740816801%29.jpg/250px-ALTer_EGO_1_18_2020_%2850740816801%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLV8"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLWA">Flashy multi-colored clothing became a trend in the early 2020s, as did baggier clothing such as hoodies, modelled here by musician <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billie_Eilish" title="Billie Eilish" id="mwLWE">Billie Eilish</a>. The 2020s revived and built upon <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000s_in_fashion#Y2K_fashion" title="2000s in fashion" id="mwLWI">Y2K fashion</a> trends.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLWM"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLWQ"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLWU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Food_delivery_robots_in_Espoo.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="In the 2020s, multiple online food delivery services such as DoorDash, Uber Eats, Postmates, Grubhub, and Just Eat Takeaway became popular, becoming popular during and after the COVID-19 pandemic. Food delivery robots also became popular in the 2020s and were finally to the point they could be used to deliver food around larger areas such as college campuses." id="mwLWY"><img alt="In the 2020s, multiple online food delivery services such as DoorDash, Uber Eats, Postmates, Grubhub, and Just Eat Takeaway became popular, becoming popular during and after the COVID-19 pandemic. Food delivery robots also became popular in the 2020s and were finally to the point they could be used to deliver food around larger areas such as college campuses." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Food_delivery_robots_in_Espoo.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Food_delivery_robots_in_Espoo.jpg/250px-Food_delivery_robots_in_Espoo.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="4608" data-file-height="3456" data-file-type="bitmap" height="139" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Food_delivery_robots_in_Espoo.jpg/500px-Food_delivery_robots_in_Espoo.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLWc"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLWg">In the 2020s, multiple online food delivery services such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DoorDash" title="DoorDash" id="mwLWk">DoorDash</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uber_Eats" title="Uber Eats" id="mwLWo">Uber Eats</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Postmates" title="Postmates" id="mwLWs">Postmates</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grubhub" title="Grubhub" id="mwLWw">Grubhub</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Just_Eat_Takeaway" title="Just Eat Takeaway" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLW0">Just Eat Takeaway</a> became popular, becoming popular during and after the COVID-19 pandemic. Food <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delivery_robot" title="Delivery robot" id="mwLW4">delivery robots</a> also became popular in the 2020s and were finally to the point they could be used to deliver food around larger areas such as college <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campus" title="Campus" id="mwLW8">campuses</a>.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLXA"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLXE"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLXI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Bluey became one of the most popular cartoons of the 2020s, along with Hazbin Hotel, Harley Quinn, Invincible, Love, Death &amp; Robots, Arcane, The Owl House, Smiling Friends, Kiff, X-Men '97, and the web series The Amazing Digital Circus." id="mwLXM"><img alt="Bluey became one of the most popular cartoons of the 2020s, along with Hazbin Hotel, Harley Quinn, Invincible, Love, Death &amp; Robots, Arcane, The Owl House, Smiling Friends, Kiff, X-Men '97, and the web series The Amazing Digital Circus." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg/250px-Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="139" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg/500px-Bluey_entertains_the_crowds_at_Under_5s_Day.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLXQ"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLXU"><i id="mwLXY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluey_(TV_series)" title="Bluey (TV series)" id="mwLXc">Bluey</a></i> became one of the most popular cartoons of the 2020s, along with <i id="mwLXg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazbin_Hotel" title="Hazbin Hotel" id="mwLXk">Hazbin Hotel</a></i>, <i id="mwLXo"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harley_Quinn_(TV_series)" title="Harley Quinn (TV series)" id="mwLXs">Harley Quinn</a></i>, <i id="mwLXw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Invincible_(TV_series)" title="Invincible (TV series)" id="mwLX0">Invincible</a></i>, <i id="mwLX4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love,_Death_&amp;_Robots" title="Love, Death &amp; Robots" id="mwLX8">Love, Death &amp; Robots</a></i>, <i id="mwLYA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arcane_(TV_series)" title="Arcane (TV series)" id="mwLYE">Arcane</a></i>, <i id="mwLYI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Owl_House" title="The Owl House" id="mwLYM">The Owl House</a></i>, <i id="mwLYQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smiling_Friends" title="Smiling Friends" id="mwLYU">Smiling Friends</a></i>, <i id="mwLYY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiff_(TV_series)" title="Kiff (TV series)" id="mwLYc">Kiff</a></i>, <i id="mwLYg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X-Men_'97" title="X-Men '97" id="mwLYk">X-Men '97</a></i>, and the web series <i id="mwLYo"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Amazing_Digital_Circus" title="The Amazing Digital Circus" id="mwLYs">The Amazing Digital Circus</a></i>.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLYw"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLY0"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLY4"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Crypto.com_arena_drone_shot_early_2023.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="The use of cryptocurrency became more mainstream in the 2020s, Crypto such as Bitcoin and others were notable. The Staples Center was even renamed Crypto.com Arena in 2021. NFTs as a form of digital art emerged in the 2020s, with NFTs such as Everydays: the First 5000 Days." id="mwLY8"><img alt="The use of cryptocurrency became more mainstream in the 2020s, Crypto such as Bitcoin and others were notable. The Staples Center was even renamed Crypto.com Arena in 2021. NFTs as a form of digital art emerged in the 2020s, with NFTs such as Everydays: the First 5000 Days." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Crypto.com_arena_drone_shot_early_2023.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Crypto.com_arena_drone_shot_early_2023.jpg/250px-Crypto.com_arena_drone_shot_early_2023.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="5280" data-file-height="2970" data-file-type="bitmap" height="104" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Crypto.com_arena_drone_shot_early_2023.jpg/500px-Crypto.com_arena_drone_shot_early_2023.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLZA"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLZE">The use of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryptocurrency" title="Cryptocurrency" id="mwLZI">cryptocurrency</a> became more mainstream in the 2020s, Crypto such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitcoin" title="Bitcoin" id="mwLZM">Bitcoin</a> and others were notable. The Staples Center was even renamed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crypto.com_Arena" title="Crypto.com Arena" id="mwLZQ">Crypto.com Arena</a> in 2021. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-fungible_token" title="Non-fungible token" id="mwLZU">NFTs</a> as a form of digital art emerged in the 2020s, with NFTs such as <i id="mwLZY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everydays:_the_First_5000_Days" title="Everydays: the First 5000 Days" id="mwLZc">Everydays: the First 5000 Days</a></i>.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLZg"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLZk"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLZo"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Galaxy_Z_series.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="5G was introduced in smartphones during the early part of the decade, with the Samsung Galaxy Flip and iPhone 12 smartphones having 5G capabilities. Foldable smartphones also became more popular, although concern grew about the durability of legacy devices." id="mwLZs"><img alt="5G was introduced in smartphones during the early part of the decade, with the Samsung Galaxy Flip and iPhone 12 smartphones having 5G capabilities. Foldable smartphones also became more popular, although concern grew about the durability of legacy devices." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Galaxy_Z_series.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Galaxy_Z_series.jpg/250px-Galaxy_Z_series.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="139" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Galaxy_Z_series.jpg/500px-Galaxy_Z_series.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLZw"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLZ0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5G" title="5G" id="mwLZ4">5G</a> was introduced in smartphones during the early part of the decade, with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samsung_Galaxy_Flip" title="Samsung Galaxy Flip" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLZ8">Samsung Galaxy Flip</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPhone_12" title="IPhone 12" id="mwLaA">iPhone 12</a> smartphones having 5G capabilities. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foldable_smartphone" title="Foldable smartphone" id="mwLaE">Foldable smartphones</a> also became more popular, although concern grew about the durability of legacy devices.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLaI"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLaM"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLaQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Chatgpt-screenshot.png" class="mw-file-description" title="Advancements in AI have been rapid and fast-paced in the 2020s. Generative AIs have become mainstream during the decade, with synthetic media in the form of Text-to-image models, DeepSeek, ChatGPT, and Audio deepfakes. Additionally, AI has been used for video creation, such as with Sora." id="mwLaU"><img alt="Advancements in AI have been rapid and fast-paced in the 2020s. Generative AIs have become mainstream during the decade, with synthetic media in the form of Text-to-image models, DeepSeek, ChatGPT, and Audio deepfakes. Additionally, AI has been used for video creation, such as with Sora." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Chatgpt-screenshot.png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Chatgpt-screenshot.png/250px-Chatgpt-screenshot.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="1280" data-file-height="768" data-file-type="bitmap" height="111" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Chatgpt-screenshot.png/500px-Chatgpt-screenshot.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLaY"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLac">Advancements in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence" title="Artificial intelligence" id="mwLag">AI</a> have been rapid and fast-paced in the 2020s. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_artificial_intelligence" title="Generative artificial intelligence" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLak">Generative AIs</a> have become mainstream during the decade, with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synthetic_media" title="Synthetic media" id="mwLao">synthetic media</a> in the form of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Text-to-image_model" title="Text-to-image model" id="mwLas">Text-to-image models</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeepSeek" title="DeepSeek" id="mwLaw">DeepSeek</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatGPT" title="ChatGPT" id="mwLa0">ChatGPT</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audio_deepfake" title="Audio deepfake" id="mwLa4">Audio deepfakes</a>. Additionally, AI has been used for video creation, such as with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sora_(text-to-video_model)" title="Sora (text-to-video model)" id="mwLa8">Sora</a>.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLbA"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLbE"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLbI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Ambassador_Burns_speaks_to_a_woman_in_front_of_a_robot.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="The Fourth Industrial Revolution in the 2020s is referred to as industrial change with emerging technologies such as AI, gene editing, and advanced robotics that blur the lines between the physical, digital, and biological worlds. Automation also continues to take over human jobs. Above is a photo of a Tesla Bot, which Tesla, Inc. hopes to begin selling by 2027." id="mwLbM"><img alt="The Fourth Industrial Revolution in the 2020s is referred to as industrial change with emerging technologies such as AI, gene editing, and advanced robotics that blur the lines between the physical, digital, and biological worlds. Automation also continues to take over human jobs. Above is a photo of a Tesla Bot, which Tesla, Inc. hopes to begin selling by 2027." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Ambassador_Burns_speaks_to_a_woman_in_front_of_a_robot.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Ambassador_Burns_speaks_to_a_woman_in_front_of_a_robot.jpg/250px-Ambassador_Burns_speaks_to_a_woman_in_front_of_a_robot.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2048" data-file-height="1366" data-file-type="bitmap" height="123" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Ambassador_Burns_speaks_to_a_woman_in_front_of_a_robot.jpg/500px-Ambassador_Burns_speaks_to_a_woman_in_front_of_a_robot.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLbQ"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLbU">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourth_Industrial_Revolution" title="Fourth Industrial Revolution" id="mwLbY">Fourth Industrial Revolution</a> in the 2020s is referred to as industrial change with emerging technologies such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence" title="Artificial intelligence" id="mwLbc">AI</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CRISPR_gene_editing" title="CRISPR gene editing" id="mwLbg">gene editing</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robotics" title="Robotics" id="mwLbk">advanced robotics</a> that blur the lines between the physical, digital, and biological worlds. Automation also continues to take over human jobs. Above is a photo of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tesla_Bot" title="Tesla Bot" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLbo">Tesla Bot</a>, which <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tesla,_Inc." title="Tesla, Inc." id="mwLbs">Tesla, Inc.</a> hopes to begin selling by 2027.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLbw"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLb0"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLb4"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Seattle_-_Lime_Bike_-_01.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Renewable energy sources such as electric vehicles as well as solar- and wind-powered devices to combat global warming became popular during the 2020s. Scooter-sharing systems have become common in the street scene of the 2020s (especially in downtown areas), with Lime becoming popular." id="mwLb8"><img alt="Renewable energy sources such as electric vehicles as well as solar- and wind-powered devices to combat global warming became popular during the 2020s. Scooter-sharing systems have become common in the street scene of the 2020s (especially in downtown areas), with Lime becoming popular." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Seattle_-_Lime_Bike_-_01.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Seattle_-_Lime_Bike_-_01.jpg/250px-Seattle_-_Lime_Bike_-_01.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="4288" data-file-height="2848" data-file-type="bitmap" height="123" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Seattle_-_Lime_Bike_-_01.jpg/500px-Seattle_-_Lime_Bike_-_01.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLcA"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLcE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renewable_energy" title="Renewable energy" id="mwLcI">Renewable energy</a> sources such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_vehicle" title="Electric vehicle" id="mwLcM">electric vehicles</a> as well as solar- and wind-powered devices to combat <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_warming" title="Global warming" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLcQ">global warming</a> became popular during the 2020s. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scooter-sharing_system" title="Scooter-sharing system" id="mwLcU">Scooter-sharing systems</a> have become common in the street scene of the 2020s (especially in downtown areas), with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(transportation_company)" title="Lime (transportation company)" id="mwLcY">Lime</a> becoming popular.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLcc"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLcg"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLck"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:French_Hill_hosts_AR_teachers_on_zoom_call.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="The early 2020s started with a rise in videoconferencing due to the pandemic, while many educational institutions and workplaces shifted to distance learning and remote work during and after the pandemic. Large-scale video conferencing became a reality and more common during the 2020s." id="mwLco"><img alt="The early 2020s started with a rise in videoconferencing due to the pandemic, while many educational institutions and workplaces shifted to distance learning and remote work during and after the pandemic. Large-scale video conferencing became a reality and more common during the 2020s." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:French_Hill_hosts_AR_teachers_on_zoom_call.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/French_Hill_hosts_AR_teachers_on_zoom_call.jpg/250px-French_Hill_hosts_AR_teachers_on_zoom_call.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="1024" data-file-height="768" data-file-type="bitmap" height="139" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/French_Hill_hosts_AR_teachers_on_zoom_call.jpg/500px-French_Hill_hosts_AR_teachers_on_zoom_call.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLcs"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLcw">The early 2020s started with a rise in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Videoconferencing" title="Videoconferencing" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLc0">videoconferencing</a> due to the pandemic, while many educational institutions and workplaces shifted to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distance_education" title="Distance education" id="mwLc4">distance learning</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Remote_work" title="Remote work" id="mwLc8">remote work</a> during and after the pandemic. Large-scale video conferencing became a reality and more common during the 2020s.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLdA"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLdE"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLdI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Marcha_de_la_&quot;Generación_Z&quot;,_15_de_Noviembre_-_54932910234.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Gen Z society grown in pop culture, such as idolization promotions and community campaigns. The Straw Hat Pirates' Jolly Roger flag from One Piece as the symbol of the chaotic Gen Z protests spread worldwide as well as media partnerships like the Operation Polaris Cross (CyberAgent–Konami agreement) and a controversial Warner–Paramount merger in Japan and the US." id="mwLdM"><img alt="Gen Z society grown in pop culture, such as idolization promotions and community campaigns. The Straw Hat Pirates' Jolly Roger flag from One Piece as the symbol of the chaotic Gen Z protests spread worldwide as well as media partnerships like the Operation Polaris Cross (CyberAgent–Konami agreement) and a controversial Warner–Paramount merger in Japan and the US." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Marcha_de_la_&quot;Generación_Z&quot;,_15_de_Noviembre_-_54932910234.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Marcha_de_la_%22Generaci%C3%B3n_Z%22%2C_15_de_Noviembre_-_54932910234.jpg/250px-Marcha_de_la_%22Generaci%C3%B3n_Z%22%2C_15_de_Noviembre_-_54932910234.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="6247" data-file-height="4165" data-file-type="bitmap" height="123" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Marcha_de_la_%22Generaci%C3%B3n_Z%22%2C_15_de_Noviembre_-_54932910234.jpg/500px-Marcha_de_la_%22Generaci%C3%B3n_Z%22%2C_15_de_Noviembre_-_54932910234.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLdQ"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLdU">Gen Z society grown in pop culture, such as idolization promotions and community campaigns. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straw_Hat_Pirates'_Jolly_Roger" title="Straw Hat Pirates' Jolly Roger" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLdY">Straw Hat Pirates' Jolly Roger</a> flag from <i id="mwLdc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Piece" title="One Piece" id="mwLdg">One Piece</a></i> as the symbol of the chaotic <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gen_Z_protests" title="Gen Z protests" id="mwLdk">Gen Z protests</a> spread worldwide as well as media partnerships like the Operation Polaris Cross (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CyberAgent" title="CyberAgent" id="mwLdo">CyberAgent</a>–<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konami" title="Konami" id="mwLds">Konami</a> agreement) and a controversial <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proposed_acquisition_of_Warner_Bros._Discovery_by_Paramount_Skydance" title="Proposed acquisition of Warner Bros. Discovery by Paramount Skydance" id="mwLdw">Warner–Paramount merger</a> in Japan and the US.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLd0"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLd4"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLd8"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cosplay_of_Tanjiro_Kamado_and_Nezuko_Kamado_from_Demon_Slayer_Kimetsu_no_Yaiba_at_FanimeCon_2023_(53056120458).jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Popular Japanese media franchises such as Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba, Chainsaw Man, Jujutsu Kaisen, Oshi no Ko, Frieren, Attack on Titan, Spy × Family, Dr. Stone, One Piece, Umamusume, Blue Lock, and Mashle reaching large international audiences and fans used for crossover works during the Reiwa era." id="mwLeA"><img alt="Popular Japanese media franchises such as Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba, Chainsaw Man, Jujutsu Kaisen, Oshi no Ko, Frieren, Attack on Titan, Spy × Family, Dr. Stone, One Piece, Umamusume, Blue Lock, and Mashle reaching large international audiences and fans used for crossover works during the Reiwa era." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cosplay_of_Tanjiro_Kamado_and_Nezuko_Kamado_from_Demon_Slayer_Kimetsu_no_Yaiba_at_FanimeCon_2023_(53056120458).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Cosplay_of_Tanjiro_Kamado_and_Nezuko_Kamado_from_Demon_Slayer_Kimetsu_no_Yaiba_at_FanimeCon_2023_%2853056120458%29.jpg/250px-Cosplay_of_Tanjiro_Kamado_and_Nezuko_Kamado_from_Demon_Slayer_Kimetsu_no_Yaiba_at_FanimeCon_2023_%2853056120458%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2048" data-file-height="1365" data-file-type="bitmap" height="123" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Cosplay_of_Tanjiro_Kamado_and_Nezuko_Kamado_from_Demon_Slayer_Kimetsu_no_Yaiba_at_FanimeCon_2023_%2853056120458%29.jpg/500px-Cosplay_of_Tanjiro_Kamado_and_Nezuko_Kamado_from_Demon_Slayer_Kimetsu_no_Yaiba_at_FanimeCon_2023_%2853056120458%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLeE"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLeI">Popular Japanese media franchises such as <i id="mwLeM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demon_Slayer:_Kimetsu_no_Yaiba" title="Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba" id="mwLeQ">Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba</a></i>, <i id="mwLeU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chainsaw_Man" title="Chainsaw Man" id="mwLeY">Chainsaw Man</a></i>, <i id="mwLec"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jujutsu_Kaisen" title="Jujutsu Kaisen" id="mwLeg">Jujutsu Kaisen</a></i>, <i id="mwLek"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oshi_no_Ko" title="Oshi no Ko" id="mwLeo">Oshi no Ko</a></i>, <i id="mwLes"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frieren" title="Frieren" id="mwLew">Frieren</a></i>, <i id="mwLe0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attack_on_Titan" title="Attack on Titan" id="mwLe4">Attack on Titan</a></i>, <i id="mwLe8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spy_×_Family" title="Spy × Family" id="mwLfA">Spy × Family</a></i>, <i id="mwLfE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dr._Stone" title="Dr. Stone" id="mwLfI">Dr. Stone</a></i>, <i id="mwLfM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Piece" title="One Piece" id="mwLfQ">One Piece</a></i>, <i id="mwLfU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umamusume:_Pretty_Derby" title="Umamusume: Pretty Derby" id="mwLfY">Umamusume</a></i>, <i id="mwLfc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Lock" title="Blue Lock" id="mwLfg">Blue Lock</a></i>, and <i id="mwLfk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mashle" title="Mashle" id="mwLfo">Mashle</a></i> reaching large international audiences and fans used for crossover works during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reiwa_era" title="Reiwa era" id="mwLfs">Reiwa era</a>.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLfw"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLf0"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLf4"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:AN19_-_Undertale_&amp;_Deltarune_-_Saturday_(33_of_35)_(48217382722).jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="The 2020s saw the online fandom boom, franchises including Deltarune, KPop Demon Hunters, Genshin Impact, Hazbin Hotel, Hatsune Miku: Colorful Stage!, Umamusume, The Amazing Digital Circus, and Heated Rivalry became highly organized and influential in the Gen Z digital culture." id="mwLf8"><img alt="The 2020s saw the online fandom boom, franchises including Deltarune, KPop Demon Hunters, Genshin Impact, Hazbin Hotel, Hatsune Miku: Colorful Stage!, Umamusume, The Amazing Digital Circus, and Heated Rivalry became highly organized and influential in the Gen Z digital culture." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:AN19_-_Undertale_&amp;_Deltarune_-_Saturday_(33_of_35)_(48217382722).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/AN19_-_Undertale_%26_Deltarune_-_Saturday_%2833_of_35%29_%2848217382722%29.jpg/250px-AN19_-_Undertale_%26_Deltarune_-_Saturday_%2833_of_35%29_%2848217382722%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2981" data-file-height="1677" data-file-type="bitmap" height="104" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/AN19_-_Undertale_%26_Deltarune_-_Saturday_%2833_of_35%29_%2848217382722%29.jpg/500px-AN19_-_Undertale_%26_Deltarune_-_Saturday_%2833_of_35%29_%2848217382722%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLgA"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLgE">The 2020s saw the online fandom boom, franchises including <i id="mwLgI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deltarune" title="Deltarune" id="mwLgM">Deltarune</a>,</i> <i id="mwLgQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KPop_Demon_Hunters" title="KPop Demon Hunters" id="mwLgU">KPop Demon Hunters</a>,</i> <i id="mwLgY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genshin_Impact" title="Genshin Impact" id="mwLgc">Genshin Impact</a></i>, <i id="mwLgg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazbin_Hotel" title="Hazbin Hotel" id="mwLgk">Hazbin Hotel</a></i>, <i id="mwLgo"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hatsune_Miku:_Colorful_Stage!" title="Hatsune Miku: Colorful Stage!" id="mwLgs">Hatsune Miku: Colorful Stage!</a></i>, <i id="mwLgw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umamusume:_Pretty_Derby" title="Umamusume: Pretty Derby" id="mwLg0">Umamusume</a></i>, <i id="mwLg4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Amazing_Digital_Circus" title="The Amazing Digital Circus" id="mwLg8">The Amazing Digital Circus</a></i>, and <i id="mwLhA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heated_Rivalry" title="Heated Rivalry" id="mwLhE">Heated Rivalry</a></i> became highly organized and influential in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generation_Z" title="Generation Z" id="mwLhI">Gen Z</a> digital culture.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLhM"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLhQ"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLhU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:HCCD25_-_TADC_group.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Independent animation entered the mainstream in the 2020s with shows such as The Amazing Digital Circus, Hazbin Hotel, Helluva Boss, Murder Drones, and Lackadaisy." id="mwLhY"><img alt="Independent animation entered the mainstream in the 2020s with shows such as The Amazing Digital Circus, Hazbin Hotel, Helluva Boss, Murder Drones, and Lackadaisy." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:HCCD25_-_TADC_group.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/HCCD25_-_TADC_group.jpg/250px-HCCD25_-_TADC_group.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2048" data-file-height="1536" data-file-type="bitmap" height="139" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/HCCD25_-_TADC_group.jpg/500px-HCCD25_-_TADC_group.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLhc"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLhg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_animation" title="Independent animation" id="mwLhk">Independent animation</a> entered the mainstream in the 2020s with shows such as <i id="mwLho"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Amazing_Digital_Circus" title="The Amazing Digital Circus" id="mwLhs">The Amazing Digital Circus</a></i>, <i id="mwLhw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazbin_Hotel" title="Hazbin Hotel" id="mwLh0">Hazbin Hotel</a></i>, <i id="mwLh4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helluva_Boss" title="Helluva Boss" id="mwLh8">Helluva Boss</a></i>, <i id="mwLiA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murder_Drones" title="Murder Drones" id="mwLiE">Murder Drones</a></i>, and <i id="mwLiI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lackadaisy_(film)" title="Lackadaisy (film)" id="mwLiM">Lackadaisy</a></i>.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLiQ"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLiU"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLiY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:空から見た大阪・関西万博2025.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="The decade saw the rise of eco-friendly wooden architecture, such as the Grand Ring by Sou Fujimoto as the symbol of the famous Expo 2025 held between April and October 2025 in Osaka." id="mwLic"><img alt="The decade saw the rise of eco-friendly wooden architecture, such as the Grand Ring by Sou Fujimoto as the symbol of the famous Expo 2025 held between April and October 2025 in Osaka." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:空から見た大阪・関西万博2025.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/%E7%A9%BA%E3%81%8B%E3%82%89%E8%A6%8B%E3%81%9F%E5%A4%A7%E9%98%AA%E3%83%BB%E9%96%A2%E8%A5%BF%E4%B8%87%E5%8D%9A2025.jpg/250px-%E7%A9%BA%E3%81%8B%E3%82%89%E8%A6%8B%E3%81%9F%E5%A4%A7%E9%98%AA%E3%83%BB%E9%96%A2%E8%A5%BF%E4%B8%87%E5%8D%9A2025.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2880" data-file-height="2160" data-file-type="bitmap" height="139" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/%E7%A9%BA%E3%81%8B%E3%82%89%E8%A6%8B%E3%81%9F%E5%A4%A7%E9%98%AA%E3%83%BB%E9%96%A2%E8%A5%BF%E4%B8%87%E5%8D%9A2025.jpg/500px-%E7%A9%BA%E3%81%8B%E3%82%89%E8%A6%8B%E3%81%9F%E5%A4%A7%E9%98%AA%E3%83%BB%E9%96%A2%E8%A5%BF%E4%B8%87%E5%8D%9A2025.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLig"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLik">The decade saw the rise of eco-friendly wooden architecture, such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Ring" title="Grand Ring" id="mwLio">Grand Ring</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sou_Fujimoto" title="Sou Fujimoto" id="mwLis">Sou Fujimoto</a> as the symbol of the famous <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expo_2025" title="Expo 2025" id="mwLiw">Expo 2025</a> held between April and October 2025 in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osaka" title="Osaka" id="mwLi0">Osaka</a>.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLi4"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLi8"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLjA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sagrada_Família_side_view.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Sagrada Familia in Barcelona became the world's tallest church when a part of its central tower was lifted into place and reached 162.91 m, surpassing Ulm Minster, made by Antonio Gaudi's longtime legacy of the construction progress since 1882." id="mwLjE"><img alt="Sagrada Familia in Barcelona became the world's tallest church when a part of its central tower was lifted into place and reached 162.91 m, surpassing Ulm Minster, made by Antonio Gaudi's longtime legacy of the construction progress since 1882." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sagrada_Família_side_view.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Sagrada_Fam%C3%ADlia_side_view.jpg/120px-Sagrada_Fam%C3%ADlia_side_view.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="3072" data-file-height="4096" data-file-type="bitmap" height="140" width="105" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Sagrada_Fam%C3%ADlia_side_view.jpg/250px-Sagrada_Fam%C3%ADlia_side_view.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLjI"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLjM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sagrada_Familia" title="Sagrada Familia" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLjQ">Sagrada Familia</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barcelona" title="Barcelona" id="mwLjU">Barcelona</a> became <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tallest_church_buildings" title="List of tallest church buildings" id="mwLjY">the world's tallest church</a> when a part of its central tower was lifted into place and reached 162.91 m, surpassing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulm_Minster" title="Ulm Minster" id="mwLjc">Ulm Minster</a>, made by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antonio_Gaudi" title="Antonio Gaudi" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLjg">Antonio Gaudi</a>'s longtime legacy of the construction progress since 1882.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLjk"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLjo"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLjs"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Épreuve_Athlétisme_Jeux_Olympiques_2024_Stade_France_-_Saint-Denis_(FR93)_-_2024-08-02_-_138.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Summer Olympic Games of the 2020s include Paris in 2024 and Los Angeles in 2028, as well as Tokyo 2020 in 2021 (the first ever Olympic games to be delayed, taking place in 2021 instead of 2020); The Winter Olympic Games of the decade included Beijing in 2022 and Milan-Cortina in 2026." id="mwLjw"><img alt="Summer Olympic Games of the 2020s include Paris in 2024 and Los Angeles in 2028, as well as Tokyo 2020 in 2021 (the first ever Olympic games to be delayed, taking place in 2021 instead of 2020); The Winter Olympic Games of the decade included Beijing in 2022 and Milan-Cortina in 2026." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Épreuve_Athlétisme_Jeux_Olympiques_2024_Stade_France_-_Saint-Denis_(FR93)_-_2024-08-02_-_138.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/%C3%89preuve_Athl%C3%A9tisme_Jeux_Olympiques_2024_Stade_France_-_Saint-Denis_%28FR93%29_-_2024-08-02_-_138.jpg/250px-%C3%89preuve_Athl%C3%A9tisme_Jeux_Olympiques_2024_Stade_France_-_Saint-Denis_%28FR93%29_-_2024-08-02_-_138.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="139" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/%C3%89preuve_Athl%C3%A9tisme_Jeux_Olympiques_2024_Stade_France_-_Saint-Denis_%28FR93%29_-_2024-08-02_-_138.jpg/500px-%C3%89preuve_Athl%C3%A9tisme_Jeux_Olympiques_2024_Stade_France_-_Saint-Denis_%28FR93%29_-_2024-08-02_-_138.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLj0"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLj4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer_Olympic_Games" title="Summer Olympic Games" id="mwLj8">Summer Olympic Games</a> of the 2020s include <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_Summer_Olympics" title="2024 Summer Olympics" id="mwLkA">Paris in 2024</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2028_Summer_Olympics" title="2028 Summer Olympics" id="mwLkE">Los Angeles in 2028</a>, as well as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Summer_Olympics" title="2020 Summer Olympics" id="mwLkI">Tokyo 2020 in 2021</a> (the first ever Olympic games to be delayed, taking place in 2021 instead of 2020); The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_Olympic_Games" title="Winter Olympic Games" id="mwLkM">Winter Olympic Games</a> of the decade included <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Winter_Olympics" title="2022 Winter Olympics" id="mwLkQ">Beijing in 2022</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Winter_Olympics" title="2026 Winter Olympics" id="mwLkU">Milan-Cortina in 2026</a>.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLkY"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLkc"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLkg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Super_Nintendo_World_(Universal_Studios_Japan).png" class="mw-file-description" title="The 2020s was a more profitable era for movies based on video games. The Super Mario Bros. Movie and its sequel surpassed $2 billion, and Nintendo plans to open a group of international theme parks called Super Nintendo World and a Nintendo Museum between 2021 and 2025." id="mwLkk"><img alt="The 2020s was a more profitable era for movies based on video games. The Super Mario Bros. Movie and its sequel surpassed $2 billion, and Nintendo plans to open a group of international theme parks called Super Nintendo World and a Nintendo Museum between 2021 and 2025." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Super_Nintendo_World_(Universal_Studios_Japan).png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Super_Nintendo_World_%28Universal_Studios_Japan%29.png/250px-Super_Nintendo_World_%28Universal_Studios_Japan%29.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="139" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Super_Nintendo_World_%28Universal_Studios_Japan%29.png/500px-Super_Nintendo_World_%28Universal_Studios_Japan%29.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLko"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLks">The 2020s was a more profitable era for movies based on video games. <i id="mwLkw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Super_Mario_Bros._Movie" title="The Super Mario Bros. Movie" id="mwLk0">The Super Mario Bros. Movie</a></i> and its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Super_Mario_Galaxy_Movie" title="The Super Mario Galaxy Movie" id="mwLk4">sequel</a> surpassed $2 billion, and Nintendo plans to open a group of international theme parks called <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Nintendo_World" title="Super Nintendo World" id="mwLk8">Super Nintendo World</a> and a Nintendo Museum between 2021 and 2025.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLlA"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLlE"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLlI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Barbenheimer_-_July_2023.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Barbenheimer, consisting of the films Barbie and Oppenheimer, was the double feature phenomenon released on the same day in July 2023, which both films became critically and commercially successful. Other films from the decade included Everything Everywhere All at Once, Wicked, Dune, Top Gun: Maverick, Sinners, Project Hail Mary, M3GAN, RRR, Backrooms, and Obsession" id="mwLlM"><img alt="Barbenheimer, consisting of the films Barbie and Oppenheimer, was the double feature phenomenon released on the same day in July 2023, which both films became critically and commercially successful. Other films from the decade included Everything Everywhere All at Once, Wicked, Dune, Top Gun: Maverick, Sinners, Project Hail Mary, M3GAN, RRR, Backrooms, and Obsession" resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Barbenheimer_-_July_2023.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Barbenheimer_-_July_2023.jpg/250px-Barbenheimer_-_July_2023.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="139" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Barbenheimer_-_July_2023.jpg/500px-Barbenheimer_-_July_2023.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLlQ"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLlU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbenheimer" title="Barbenheimer" id="mwLlY">Barbenheimer</a>, consisting of the films <i id="mwLlc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbie_(film)" title="Barbie (film)" id="mwLlg">Barbie</a></i> and <i id="mwLlk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oppenheimer_(film)" title="Oppenheimer (film)" id="mwLlo">Oppenheimer</a></i>, was the double feature phenomenon released on the same day in July 2023, which both films became critically and commercially successful. Other films from the decade included <i id="mwLls"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everything_Everywhere_All_at_Once" title="Everything Everywhere All at Once" id="mwLlw">Everything Everywhere All at Once</a></i>, <i id="mwLl0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wicked_(2024_film)" title="Wicked (2024 film)" id="mwLl4">Wicked</a></i>, <i id="mwLl8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dune_(2021_film)" title="Dune (2021 film)" id="mwLmA">Dune</a></i>, <i id="mwLmE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Top_Gun:_Maverick" title="Top Gun: Maverick" id="mwLmI">Top Gun: Maverick</a></i>, <i id="mwLmM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinners_(2025_film)" title="Sinners (2025 film)" id="mwLmQ">Sinners</a></i>, <i id="mwLmU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_Hail_Mary_(film)" title="Project Hail Mary (film)" id="mwLmY">Project Hail Mary</a></i>, <i id="mwLmc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M3GAN" title="M3GAN" id="mwLmg">M3GAN</a></i>, <i id="mwLmk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RRR" title="RRR" id="mwLmo">RRR</a></i>, <i id="mwLms"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backrooms_(film)" title="Backrooms (film)" id="mwLmw">Backrooms</a></i>, and <i id="mwLm0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Obsession_(2025_film)" title="Obsession (2025 film)" id="mwLm4">Obsession</a></i></div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLm8"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLnA"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLnE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:AR-_Apple_Vision_Pro_(2023).png" class="mw-file-description" title="Apple Vision Pro, which was released in 2024, marks an advancement in spatial computing and mixed reality headsets. The device intends to merge physical and digital environments, overlaying computer graphics on each individual user's real-world environments." id="mwLnI"><img alt="Apple Vision Pro, which was released in 2024, marks an advancement in spatial computing and mixed reality headsets. The device intends to merge physical and digital environments, overlaying computer graphics on each individual user's real-world environments." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:AR-_Apple_Vision_Pro_(2023).png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/AR-_Apple_Vision_Pro_%282023%29.png/250px-AR-_Apple_Vision_Pro_%282023%29.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="2160" data-file-height="1620" data-file-type="bitmap" height="139" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/AR-_Apple_Vision_Pro_%282023%29.png/500px-AR-_Apple_Vision_Pro_%282023%29.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLnM"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLnQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Vision_Pro" title="Apple Vision Pro" id="mwLnU">Apple Vision Pro</a>, which was released in 2024, marks an advancement in spatial computing and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mixed_reality" title="Mixed reality" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLnY">mixed reality</a> headsets. The device intends to merge physical and digital environments, overlaying computer graphics on each individual user's real-world environments.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLnc"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLng"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLnk"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Monkey_in_the_Matrix_(52536941713).jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="During the 2020s, the idea of brain implants existed in an early, limited form. The company Neuralink and a research group demonstrated the ability for a monkey to move a computer cursor with neural signals, typing coherent sentences." id="mwLno"><img alt="During the 2020s, the idea of brain implants existed in an early, limited form. The company Neuralink and a research group demonstrated the ability for a monkey to move a computer cursor with neural signals, typing coherent sentences." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Monkey_in_the_Matrix_(52536941713).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Monkey_in_the_Matrix_%2852536941713%29.jpg/250px-Monkey_in_the_Matrix_%2852536941713%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="3354" data-file-height="3174" data-file-type="bitmap" height="140" width="148" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Monkey_in_the_Matrix_%2852536941713%29.jpg/330px-Monkey_in_the_Matrix_%2852536941713%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLns"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLnw">During the 2020s, the idea of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brain_implant" title="Brain implant" id="mwLn0">brain implants</a> existed in an early, limited form. The company <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuralink" title="Neuralink" id="mwLn4">Neuralink</a> and a research group demonstrated the ability for a monkey to move a computer cursor with neural signals, typing coherent sentences.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLn8"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLoA"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLoE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cloud_Logo.png" class="mw-file-description" title="Cloud computing has surged in popularity following and during the global pandemic of 2020. Cloud computing allows for data to be stored in data centres and looked up on any device, rather than the photos, notes, etc. of a device being restricted to just that device." id="mwLoI"><img alt="Cloud computing has surged in popularity following and during the global pandemic of 2020. Cloud computing allows for data to be stored in data centres and looked up on any device, rather than the photos, notes, etc. of a device being restricted to just that device." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cloud_Logo.png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Cloud_Logo.png/250px-Cloud_Logo.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="2000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="140" width="140" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Cloud_Logo.png/330px-Cloud_Logo.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLoM"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLoQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloud_computing" title="Cloud computing" id="mwLoU">Cloud computing</a> has surged in popularity following and during the global pandemic of 2020. Cloud computing allows for data to be stored in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_center" title="Data center" id="mwLoY">data centres</a> and looked up on any device, rather than the photos, notes, etc. of a device being restricted to just that device.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLoc"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLog"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLok"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sustainable_Development_Goals.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="The Sustainable Development Goals promote seventeen interlinked objectives designed to serve as a &quot;shared blueprint for peace and prosperity for people and the planet, now and into the future&quot;. Pictured above is a diagram listing the 17 Sustainable Development Goals, which are intended to be completed by the end of the 2020s." id="mwLoo"><img alt="The Sustainable Development Goals promote seventeen interlinked objectives designed to serve as a &quot;shared blueprint for peace and prosperity for people and the planet, now and into the future&quot;. Pictured above is a diagram listing the 17 Sustainable Development Goals, which are intended to be completed by the end of the 2020s." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sustainable_Development_Goals.svg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Sustainable_Development_Goals.svg/250px-Sustainable_Development_Goals.svg.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="512" data-file-height="324" data-file-type="drawing" height="117" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Sustainable_Development_Goals.svg/500px-Sustainable_Development_Goals.svg.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLos"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLow">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sustainable_Development_Goals" title="Sustainable Development Goals" id="mwLo0">Sustainable Development Goals</a> promote seventeen interlinked objectives designed to serve as a "shared blueprint for peace and prosperity for people and the planet, now and into the future". Pictured above is a diagram listing the 17 Sustainable Development Goals, which are intended to be completed by the end of the 2020s.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLo4"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLo8"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLpA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Meta_Headquarters_Sign.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Social media rebranding occurred during the 2020s, with Facebook, Inc. and Twitter changing their names to Meta Platforms and X (though many people continue to call it Twitter). New social platforms such as Threads and Bluesky also launched." id="mwLpE"><img alt="Social media rebranding occurred during the 2020s, with Facebook, Inc. and Twitter changing their names to Meta Platforms and X (though many people continue to call it Twitter). New social platforms such as Threads and Bluesky also launched." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Meta_Headquarters_Sign.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Meta_Headquarters_Sign.jpg/250px-Meta_Headquarters_Sign.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="1080" data-file-height="810" data-file-type="bitmap" height="139" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Meta_Headquarters_Sign.jpg/500px-Meta_Headquarters_Sign.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLpI"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLpM">Social media rebranding occurred during the 2020s, with Facebook, Inc. and Twitter changing their names to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_Platforms" title="Meta Platforms" id="mwLpQ">Meta Platforms</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X_(social_network)" title="X (social network)" id="mwLpU">X</a> (though many people continue to call it Twitter). New social platforms such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Threads_(social_network)" title="Threads (social network)" id="mwLpY">Threads</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluesky" title="Bluesky" id="mwLpc">Bluesky</a> also launched.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLpg"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLpk"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLpo"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:The_White_House_-_54437612258.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Japanese baseball player Shohei Otani became one of the most popular sports figures during the decade, following the victory of the Los Angeles Dodgers at the 2024 World Series, and again in 2025 followed by Yoshinobu Yamamoto who won the World Series MVP." id="mwLps"><img alt="Japanese baseball player Shohei Otani became one of the most popular sports figures during the decade, following the victory of the Los Angeles Dodgers at the 2024 World Series, and again in 2025 followed by Yoshinobu Yamamoto who won the World Series MVP." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:The_White_House_-_54437612258.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/The_White_House_-_54437612258.jpg/250px-The_White_House_-_54437612258.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="123" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/The_White_House_-_54437612258.jpg/500px-The_White_House_-_54437612258.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLpw"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLp0">Japanese baseball player <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shohei_Otani" title="Shohei Otani" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLp4">Shohei Otani</a> became one of the most popular sports figures during the decade, following the victory of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Angeles_Dodgers" title="Los Angeles Dodgers" id="mwLp8">Los Angeles Dodgers</a> at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_World_Series" title="2024 World Series" id="mwLqA">2024 World Series</a>, and again in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_World_Series" title="2025 World Series" id="mwLqE">2025</a> followed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshinobu_Yamamoto" title="Yoshinobu Yamamoto" id="mwLqI">Yoshinobu Yamamoto</a> who won the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Series_Most_Valuable_Player_Award" title="World Series Most Valuable Player Award" id="mwLqM">World Series MVP</a>.</div></li>
<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 220px;" id="mwLqQ"><div class="thumb" style="width: 215px; height: 170px;" id="mwLqU"><span typeof="mw:File" id="mwLqY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Spain_World_Cup_Winners_Argentina_v_Spain_19_July_2026-1.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Football domination continued during the decade, including Argentina won over France at the 2022 FIFA World Cup final. Lamine Yamal, Lionel Messi, and Kylian Mbappé became one of the famous footballers of the decade, both they returned popularity and Spain won in 2026 since 2010." id="mwLqc"><img alt="Football domination continued during the decade, including Argentina won over France at the 2022 FIFA World Cup final. Lamine Yamal, Lionel Messi, and Kylian Mbappé became one of the famous footballers of the decade, both they returned popularity and Spain won in 2026 since 2010." resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Spain_World_Cup_Winners_Argentina_v_Spain_19_July_2026-1.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Spain_World_Cup_Winners_Argentina_v_Spain_19_July_2026-1.jpg/250px-Spain_World_Cup_Winners_Argentina_v_Spain_19_July_2026-1.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="5000" data-file-height="3333" data-file-type="bitmap" height="123" width="185" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Spain_World_Cup_Winners_Argentina_v_Spain_19_July_2026-1.jpg/500px-Spain_World_Cup_Winners_Argentina_v_Spain_19_July_2026-1.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLqg"></a></span></div><div class="gallerytext" id="mwLqk">Football domination continued during the decade, including Argentina won over France at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_FIFA_World_Cup_final" title="2022 FIFA World Cup final" id="mwLqo">2022 FIFA World Cup final</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamine_Yamal" title="Lamine Yamal" id="mwLqs">Lamine Yamal</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lionel_Messi" title="Lionel Messi" id="mwLqw">Lionel Messi</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kylian_Mbappé" title="Kylian Mbappé" id="mwLq0">Kylian Mbappé</a> became one of the famous footballers of the decade, both they returned popularity and Spain won in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_FIFA_World_Cup_final" title="2026 FIFA World Cup final" id="mwLq4">2026</a> since 2010.</div></li>
</ul>

<section data-mw-section-id="54" id="mwLq8" aria-labelledby="Fashion"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Fashion">Fashion</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=54" title="Edit section: Fashion"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3694" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLrA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2020s in fashion&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt3695" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt3694" id="mwLrE">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020s_in_fashion" title="2020s in fashion">2020s in fashion</a></div>

<p id="mwLrI">The fashion of the early 2020s was characterized by a variety of styles and influences from different eras. During this period, the trend towards individuality and self-expression in clothing continued. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zillennials" title="Zillennials" id="mwLrM">Young millennials</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generation_Z" title="Generation Z" id="mwLrQ">Generation Z</a> has witnessed and enjoyed a notable resurgence of fashion styles from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1980s_in_fashion" title="1980s in fashion" id="mwLrU">1980s</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1990s_in_fashion" title="1990s in fashion" id="mwLrY">1990s</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000s_in_fashion" title="2000s in fashion" id="mwLrc">2000s</a> in the fashion industry. A prominent example of this is the revival of trends such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crop_tops" title="Crop tops" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLrg">crop tops</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baggy_jeans" title="Baggy jeans" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLrk">baggy jeans</a>, and elements from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000s_in_fashion#Y2K_fashion" title="2000s in fashion" id="mwLro">Y2K</a> aesthetic.<sup about="#mwt3698" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-YPulse_Bringing_Back_995-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;YPulse Bringing Back&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-YPulse_Bringing_Back-995&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-YPulse_Bringing_Back-995" id="mwLrs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLrw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLr0">[</span>995<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLr4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3701" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-996" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-996&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-996" id="mwLr8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLsA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLsE">[</span>996<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLsI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwLsM">In the 2020s, many companies, including current <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fast_fashion" title="Fast fashion" id="mwLsQ">fast fashion</a> giants such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shein_(company)" title="Shein (company)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLsU">Shein</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temu_(marketplace)" title="Temu (marketplace)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLsY">Temu</a>, began using social media platforms such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TikTok" title="TikTok" id="mwLsc">TikTok</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instagram" title="Instagram" id="mwLsg">Instagram</a> as a marketing tool.<sup about="#mwt3704" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-997" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-997&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-997" id="mwLsk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLso"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLss">[</span>997<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLsw">]</span></span></a></sup> Marketing strategies involving third parties, particularly <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Influencers" title="Influencers" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLs0">influencers</a> and celebrities, have become prominent tactics. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E-commerce" title="E-commerce" id="mwLs4">E-commerce</a> platforms that promote small businesses, such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Depop" title="Depop" id="mwLs8">Depop</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etsy" title="Etsy" id="mwLtA">Etsy</a>, grew by offering vintage, homemade, or resold clothing from individual sellers.<sup about="#mwt3707" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-998" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-998&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-998" id="mwLtE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLtI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLtM">[</span>998<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLtQ">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charity_shop" title="Charity shop" id="mwLtU">Thrifting</a> also exploded in popularity because of the potential to find valuable pieces of clothing at cheaper prices.<sup about="#mwt3710" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-999" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-999&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-999" id="mwLtY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLtc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLtg">[</span>999<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLtk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="55" id="mwLto" aria-labelledby="Film"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Film">Film</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=55" title="Edit section: Film"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3711" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLts" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2020s in film&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt3712" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt3711" id="mwLtw">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020s_in_film" title="2020s in film">2020s in film</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwLt0"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Avatar_The_Way_of_Water_Tokyo_Press_Conference_Jon_Landau,_Sam_Worthington,_Zoe_Saldaña,_James_Cameron,_Sigourney_Weaver_&amp;_Stephen_Lang_(52562966421).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwLt4"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Avatar_The_Way_of_Water_Tokyo_Press_Conference_Jon_Landau,_Sam_Worthington,_Zoe_Saldaña,_James_Cameron,_Sigourney_Weaver_&amp;_Stephen_Lang_(52562966421).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Avatar_The_Way_of_Water_Tokyo_Press_Conference_Jon_Landau%2C_Sam_Worthington%2C_Zoe_Salda%C3%B1a%2C_James_Cameron%2C_Sigourney_Weaver_%26_Stephen_Lang_%2852562966421%29.jpg/250px-Avatar_The_Way_of_Water_Tokyo_Press_Conference_Jon_Landau%2C_Sam_Worthington%2C_Zoe_Salda%C3%B1a%2C_James_Cameron%2C_Sigourney_Weaver_%26_Stephen_Lang_%2852562966421%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="6000" data-file-height="4000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Avatar_The_Way_of_Water_Tokyo_Press_Conference_Jon_Landau%2C_Sam_Worthington%2C_Zoe_Salda%C3%B1a%2C_James_Cameron%2C_Sigourney_Weaver_%26_Stephen_Lang_%2852562966421%29.jpg/500px-Avatar_The_Way_of_Water_Tokyo_Press_Conference_Jon_Landau%2C_Sam_Worthington%2C_Zoe_Salda%C3%B1a%2C_James_Cameron%2C_Sigourney_Weaver_%26_Stephen_Lang_%2852562966421%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwLt8"></a><figcaption id="mwLuA">The highest-grossing films of the decade so far are <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Cameron" title="James Cameron" id="mwLuE">James Cameron</a>'s <i id="mwLuI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avatar:_The_Way_of_Water" title="Avatar: The Way of Water" id="mwLuM">Avatar: The Way of Water</a></i> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jiaozi_(director)" title="Jiaozi (director)" id="mwLuQ">Jiaozi</a>'s <i id="mwLuU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ne_Zha_2" title="Ne Zha 2" id="mwLuY">Ne Zha 2</a></i>.<sup about="#mwt3715" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BOM_1000-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;BOM&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-BOM-1000&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-BOM-1000" id="mwLuc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLug"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLuk">[</span>1000<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLuo">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwLus">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impact_of_the_COVID-19_pandemic_on_cinema" title="Impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on cinema" id="mwLuw">COVID-19 pandemic heavily impacted film releases</a> especially early in the decade, resulting in a drastic drop in box office revenue as well as many films postponing their release or shifting it to a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Streaming_media" title="Streaming media" id="mwLu0">streaming services</a>. <i id="mwLu4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avatar:_The_Way_of_Water" title="Avatar: The Way of Water" id="mwLu8">Avatar: The Way of Water</a></i> is the highest-grossing film of the decade so far, and currently the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_highest-grossing_films" title="List of highest-grossing films" id="mwLvA">third-highest-grossing film of all time</a>. Other financially successful films at the box office include <i id="mwLvE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Top_Gun:_Maverick" title="Top Gun: Maverick" id="mwLvI">Top Gun: Maverick</a></i>, <i id="mwLvM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dune_(2021_film)" title="Dune (2021 film)" id="mwLvQ">Dune</a></i> and its sequel <i id="mwLvU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dune:_Part_Two" title="Dune: Part Two" id="mwLvY">Dune: Part Two</a></i>, and <i id="mwLvc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wicked_(2024_film)" title="Wicked (2024 film)" id="mwLvg">Wicked</a></i>. Superhero films mostly continued to do well financially, such as most successes from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvel_Cinematic_Universe" title="Marvel Cinematic Universe" id="mwLvk">Marvel Cinematic Universe</a>, continuing with its "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Marvel_Cinematic_Universe_films#The_Multiverse_Saga" title="List of Marvel Cinematic Universe films" id="mwLvo">Multiverse Saga</a>" (accompanied with a series of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Marvel_Cinematic_Universe_television_series_(Marvel_Studios)" title="List of Marvel Cinematic Universe television series (Marvel Studios)" id="mwLvs">shows</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvel's_Special_Presentations" title="Marvel's Special Presentations" id="mwLvw">specials</a> created exclusively on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disney+" title="Disney+" id="mwLv0">Disney+</a> which interconnect with the films). Several successful horror films included <i id="mwLv4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M3GAN" title="M3GAN" id="mwLv8">M3GAN</a></i>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X_(film_series)" title="X (film series)" id="mwLwA"><i id="mwLwE">X</i> trilogy</a>, <i id="mwLwI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbarian_(2022_film)" title="Barbarian (2022 film)" id="mwLwM">Barbarian</a></i>, and <i id="mwLwQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinners_(2025_film)" title="Sinners (2025 film)" id="mwLwU">Sinners</a></i>.<sup about="#mwt3718" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1001" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-1001&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-1001" id="mwLwY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLwc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLwg">[</span>1001<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLwk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwLwo">In 2023, the films <i id="mwLws"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbie_(film)" title="Barbie (film)" id="mwLww">Barbie</a></i> and <i id="mwLw0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oppenheimer_(film)" title="Oppenheimer (film)" id="mwLw4">Oppenheimer</a></i> were both released on the same day, which led to the creation of the double feature phenomenon known as "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbenheimer" title="Barbenheimer" id="mwLw8">Barbenheimer</a>". Both films became critically and commercially successful with both receiving a nomination for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture" title="Academy Award for Best Picture" id="mwLxA">Best Picture</a> at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/96th_Academy_Awards" title="96th Academy Awards" id="mwLxE">96th Academy Awards</a>, and the latter winning both the award and nabbing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christopher_Nolan" title="Christopher Nolan" id="mwLxI">Christopher Nolan</a>'s first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academy_Award_for_Best_Director" title="Academy Award for Best Director" id="mwLxM">Best Director</a> award.</p>

<p id="mwLxQ">2025 became the year of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_highest-grossing_animated_films" title="List of highest-grossing animated films" id="mwLxU">highest-grossing animated films</a> in Asia, such as <i id="mwLxY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ne_Zha_2" title="Ne Zha 2" id="mwLxc">Ne Zha 2</a></i> and <i id="mwLxg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demon_Slayer:_Kimetsu_no_Yaiba_–_The_Movie:_Infinity_Castle" title="Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba – The Movie: Infinity Castle" id="mwLxk">Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba – The Movie: Infinity Castle</a></i>, to gross $3 billion in a successful box office of the year, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinema_of_Japan" title="Cinema of Japan" id="mwLxo">Japanese anime films</a> became dominant for 15 years since <i id="mwLxs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrietty" title="Arrietty" id="mwLxw">Arrietty</a></i> (2010).<sup about="#mwt3721" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1002" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-1002&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-1002" id="mwLx0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLx4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLx8">[</span>1002<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLyA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3724" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto2_1003-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;auto2&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-auto2-1003&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-auto2-1003" id="mwLyE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLyI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLyM">[</span>1003<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLyQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<p id="mwLyU">
<!--{| class="wikitable"
! style="width:9%"| Year
! style="width:9%"| 2020
|&#x2D;
| rowspan=2| '''Highest grossing by release year'''
|
|&#x2D;
|
|&#x2D;
|'''Academy Award for Best Picture winners'''
|
|}-->
<br id="mwLyY"></p>
</section><section data-mw-section-id="56" id="mwLyc" aria-labelledby="Television"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Television">Television</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=56" title="Edit section: Television"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><!--Avoid favoritism by not mentioning specific TV shows. Keep in mind that this subsection is merely a summary and not an advertising a television show or place to list your favorite television shows. This is mostly for long&#x2D;term, observed trends and styles.-->
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3725" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLyg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2020s in television&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt3726" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt3725" id="mwLyk">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020s_in_television" title="2020s in television" class="mw-redirect">2020s in television</a></div>

<p id="mwLyo">The 2020s started off with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Streaming_services" title="Streaming services" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLys">streaming services</a> like <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netflix" title="Netflix" id="mwLyw">Netflix</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Prime_Video" title="Amazon Prime Video" id="mwLy0">Amazon Prime Video</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_TV+" title="Apple TV+" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLy4">Apple TV+</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paramount+" title="Paramount+" id="mwLy8">Paramount+</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HBO_Max" title="HBO Max" id="mwLzA">HBO Max</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Showtime_(TV_network)" title="Showtime (TV network)" id="mwLzE">Showtime</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crunchyroll" title="Crunchyroll" id="mwLzI">Crunchyroll</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hayu_(streaming_service)" title="Hayu (streaming service)" id="mwLzM">Hayu</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peacock_(streaming_service)" title="Peacock (streaming service)" id="mwLzQ">Peacock</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DAZN" title="DAZN" id="mwLzU">DAZN</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disney+" title="Disney+" id="mwLzY">Disney+</a>. Ad-supported <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Streaming_television" title="Streaming television" id="mwLzc">streaming televisions</a> such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pluto_TV" title="Pluto TV" id="mwLzg">Pluto TV</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube_TV" title="YouTube TV" id="mwLzk">YouTube TV</a> also became more popular.</p>

<p id="mwLzo">During a live broadcast of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/94th_Academy_Awards" title="94th Academy Awards" id="mwLzs">94th Academy Awards</a> in 2022, audiences across the auditorium and at home watched in shock as actor and musician <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Will_Smith" title="Will Smith" id="mwLzw">Will Smith</a>, who was nominated for, and won, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academy_Award_for_Best_Actor" title="Academy Award for Best Actor" id="mwLz0">Best Actor</a> that evening for his performance in the biographical film <i id="mwLz4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Richard_(film)" title="King Richard (film)" id="mwLz8">King Richard</a></i>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Rock–Will_Smith_slapping_incident" title="Chris Rock–Will Smith slapping incident" id="mwL0A">slapped</a> comedian and actor <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Rock" title="Chris Rock" id="mwL0E">Chris Rock</a>, who was presenting <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academy_Award_for_Best_Documentary_Feature" title="Academy Award for Best Documentary Feature" class="mw-redirect" id="mwL0I">Best Documentary Feature</a>, across the face after making a joke about Smith's wife <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jada_Pinkett_Smith" title="Jada Pinkett Smith" id="mwL0M">Jada Pinkett Smith</a>. Following that ceremony's incident, after receiving his Oscar, Smith was suspended from the academy for ten years.</p>

<p id="mwL0Q">Billions of people watched the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_and_state_funeral_of_Elizabeth_II" title="Death and state funeral of Elizabeth II" id="mwL0U">death and state funeral of Elizabeth II</a> in 2022 and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_Summer_Olympics" title="2024 Summer Olympics" id="mwL0Y">2024 Summer Olympics</a> coverage in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris" title="Paris" id="mwL0c">Paris</a> speculated to be the most watched special television events in history.<sup about="#mwt3729" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1004" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-1004&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-1004" id="mwL0g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwL0k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwL0o">[</span>1004<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwL0s">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3732" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1005" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-1005&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-1005" id="mwL0w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwL00"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwL04">[</span>1005<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwL08">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="57" id="mwL1A" aria-labelledby="Animated"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Animated">Animated</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=57" title="Edit section: Animated"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwL1E">Japanese <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anime" title="Anime" id="mwL1I">anime</a> continued to rise in global popularity and appeal during the decade,<sup about="#mwt3735" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1006" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-1006&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-1006" id="mwL1M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwL1Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwL1U">[</span>1006<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwL1Y">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3738" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1007" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-1007&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-1007" id="mwL1c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwL1g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwL1k">[</span>1007<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwL1o">]</span></span></a></sup> with works such as <i id="mwL1s"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jujutsu_Kaisen_(TV_series)" title="Jujutsu Kaisen (TV series)" id="mwL1w">Jujutsu Kaisen</a></i>, <i id="mwL10"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demon_Slayer:_Kimetsu_no_Yaiba_(TV_series)" title="Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV series)" id="mwL14">Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba</a></i>, <i id="mwL18"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beastars" title="Beastars" id="mwL2A">Beastars</a></i>, <i id="mwL2E"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chainsaw_Man_(TV_series)" title="Chainsaw Man (TV series)" id="mwL2I">Chainsaw Man</a></i>, <i id="mwL2M"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spy_×_Family_(TV_series)" title="Spy × Family (TV series)" id="mwL2Q">Spy × Family</a></i>, <i id="mwL2U"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyberpunk:_Edgerunners" title="Cyberpunk: Edgerunners" id="mwL2Y">Cyberpunk: Edgerunners</a></i>, <i id="mwL2c"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hell's_Paradise_(TV_series)" title="Hell's Paradise (TV series)" id="mwL2g">Hell's Paradise: Jigokuraku</a></i>, <i id="mwL2k"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oshi_no_Ko" title="Oshi no Ko" id="mwL2o">Oshi no Ko</a></i>, <i id="mwL2s"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baki_the_Grappler" title="Baki the Grappler" id="mwL2w">Baki</a></i>, <i id="mwL20"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delicious_in_Dungeon" title="Delicious in Dungeon" id="mwL24">Delicious in Dungeon</a></i>, <i id="mwL28"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Record_of_Ragnarok" title="Record of Ragnarok" id="mwL3A">Record of Ragnarok</a></i>, <i id="mwL3E"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frieren" title="Frieren" id="mwL3I">Frieren</a></i>, <i id="mwL3M"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dandadan" title="Dandadan" id="mwL3Q">Dandadan</a></i>, <i id="mwL3U"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solo_Leveling" title="Solo Leveling" id="mwL3Y">Solo Leveling</a></i>, <i id="mwL3c"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scott_Pilgrim_Takes_Off" title="Scott Pilgrim Takes Off" id="mwL3g">Scott Pilgrim Takes Off</a></i>, <i id="mwL3k"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo_Revengers" title="Tokyo Revengers" id="mwL3o">Tokyo Revengers</a></i>, <i id="mwL3s"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinland_Saga_(TV_series)" title="Vinland Saga (TV series)" id="mwL3w">Vinland Saga</a></i>, <i id="mwL30"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Witch_Watch" title="Witch Watch" id="mwL34">Witch Watch</a></i>, <i id="mwL38"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaiju_No._8" title="Kaiju No. 8" id="mwL4A">Kaiju No. 8</a></i>, <i id="mwL4E"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gachiakuta" title="Gachiakuta" id="mwL4I">Gachiakuta</a></i>, <i id="mwL4M"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bleach:_Thousand-Year_Blood_War" title="Bleach: Thousand-Year Blood War" id="mwL4Q">Bleach: Thousand-Year Blood War</a></i>, <i id="mwL4U"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sakamoto_Days" title="Sakamoto Days" id="mwL4Y">Sakamoto Days</a></i>, <i id="mwL4c"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attack_on_Titan_(TV_series)" title="Attack on Titan (TV series)" id="mwL4g">Attack on Titan</a></i>, <i id="mwL4k"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JoJo's_Bizarre_Adventure_(TV_series)" title="JoJo's Bizarre Adventure (TV series)" id="mwL4o">Jojo's Bizarre Adventure</a></i> and <i id="mwL4s"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Piece_(1999_TV_series)" title="One Piece (1999 TV series)" id="mwL4w">One Piece</a></i> reaching large international audiences.</p>

<p id="mwL40">New and critically acclaimed teen and adult animated shows like <i id="mwL44"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harley_Quinn_(TV_series)" title="Harley Quinn (TV series)" id="mwL48">Harley Quinn</a></i>, <i id="mwL5A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazbin_Hotel" title="Hazbin Hotel" id="mwL5E">Hazbin Hotel</a></i>, <i id="mwL5I"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primal_(TV_series)" title="Primal (TV series)" id="mwL5M">Primal</a></i>, <i id="mwL5Q"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love,_Death_&amp;_Robots" title="Love, Death &amp; Robots" id="mwL5U">Love, Death &amp; Robots</a></i>, <i id="mwL5Y"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_of_Zeus" title="Blood of Zeus" id="mwL5c">Blood of Zeus</a></i>, <i id="mwL5g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Invincible_(TV_series)" title="Invincible (TV series)" id="mwL5k">Invincible</a></i>, <i id="mwL5o"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arcane_(TV_series)" title="Arcane (TV series)" id="mwL5s">Arcane</a></i>, <i id="mwL5w"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil_May_Cry_(TV_series)" title="Devil May Cry (TV series)" id="mwL50">Devil May Cry</a></i>, and <i id="mwL54"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smiling_Friends" title="Smiling Friends" id="mwL58">Smiling Friends</a></i>, as well as  the web series <i id="mwL6A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Amazing_Digital_Circus" title="The Amazing Digital Circus" id="mwL6E">The Amazing Digital Circus</a></i>, were launched in the 2020s, along with other animated shows such as <i id="mwL6I"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluey_(TV_series)" title="Bluey (TV series)" id="mwL6M">Bluey</a></i>, <i id="mwL6Q"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batwheels" title="Batwheels" id="mwL6U">Batwheels</a></i>, <i id="mwL6Y"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilda_(TV_series)" title="Hilda (TV series)" id="mwL6c">Hilda</a></i>,  <i id="mwL6g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Owl_House" title="The Owl House" id="mwL6k">The Owl House</a></i>, <i id="mwL6o"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiff_(TV_series)" title="Kiff (TV series)" id="mwL6s">Kiff</a></i>, <i id="mwL6w"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X-Men_'97" title="X-Men '97" id="mwL60">X-Men '97</a></i>, <i id="mwL64"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphibia_(TV_series)" title="Amphibia (TV series)" id="mwL68">Amphibia</a></i>, and <i id="mwL7A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Wars:_Visions" title="Star Wars: Visions" id="mwL7E">Star Wars: Visions</a></i>.<sup about="#mwt3741" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1008" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-1008&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-1008" id="mwL7I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwL7M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwL7Q">[</span>1008<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwL7U">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="58" id="mwL7Y" aria-labelledby="Live-action"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Live-action">Live-action</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2020s&amp;action=edit&amp;section=58" title="Edit section: Live-action"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwL7c">A variety of shows on streaming services such as <i id="mwL7g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squid_Game" title="Squid Game" id="mwL7k">Squid Game</a></i>, <i id="mwL7o"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Severance_(TV_series)" title="Severance (TV series)" id="mwL7s">Severance</a></i>, <i id="mwL7w"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Never_Have_I_Ever_(TV_series)" title="Never Have I Ever (TV series)" id="mwL70">Never Have I Ever</a></i>, <i id="mwL74"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tulsa_King" title="Tulsa King" id="mwL78">Tulsa King</a></i>, <i id="mwL8A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ted_Lasso" title="Ted Lasso" id="mwL8E">Ted Lasso</a></i>, <i id="mwL8I"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beef_(TV_series)" title="Beef (TV series)" id="mwL8M">Beef</a></i>, <i id="mwL8Q"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Boys_(TV_series)" title="The Boys (TV series)" id="mwL8U">The Boys</a></i>, <i id="mwL8Y"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extraordinary_Attorney_Woo" title="Extraordinary Attorney Woo" id="mwL8c">Extraordinary Attorney Woo</a></i>, <i id="mwL8g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Only_Murders_in_the_Building" title="Only Murders in the Building" id="mwL8k">Only Murders in the Building</a></i>, <i id="mwL8o"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wednesday_(TV_series)" title="Wednesday (TV series)" id="mwL8s">Wednesday</a></i>, <i id="mwL8w"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sex_Lives_of_College_Girls" title="The Sex Lives of College Girls" id="mwL80">The Sex Lives of College Girls</a></i>, <i id="mwL84"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euphoria_(American_TV_series)" title="Euphoria (American TV series)" id="mwL88">Euphoria</a></i>, <i id="mwL9A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbott_Elementary" title="Abbott Elementary" id="mwL9E">Abbott Elementary</a></i>, <i id="mwL9I"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bear_(TV_series)" title="The Bear (TV series)" id="mwL9M">The Bear</a></i>, <i id="mwL9Q"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heartstopper_(TV_series)" title="Heartstopper (TV series)" id="mwL9U">Heartstopper</a></i>, <i id="mwL9Y"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love,_Victor" title="Love, Victor" id="mwL9c">Love, Victor</a></i>, <i id="mwL9g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pitt" title="The Pitt" id="mwL9k">The Pitt</a></i>, <i id="mwL9o"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shōgun_(2024_TV_series)" title="Shōgun (2024 TV series)" id="mwL9s">Shōgun</a></i>, <i id="mwL9w"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Witcher_(TV_series)" title="The Witcher (TV series)" id="mwL90">The Witcher</a></i>, <i id="mwL94"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_White_Lotus" title="The White Lotus" id="mwL98">The White Lotus</a></i>, <i id="mwL-A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alice_in_Borderland_(TV_series)" title="Alice in Borderland (TV series)" id="mwL-E">Alice in Borderland</a></i>, <i id="mwL-I"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hacks_(TV_series)" title="Hacks (TV series)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwL-M">Hacks</a></i>, <i id="mwL-Q"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Diplomat_(American_TV_series)" title="The Diplomat (American TV series)" id="mwL-U">The Diplomat</a></i>, <i id="mwL-Y"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellowstone_(American_TV_series)" title="Yellowstone (American TV series)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwL-c">Yellowstone</a></i>, <i id="mwL-g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Last_of_Us_(TV_series)" title="The Last of Us (TV series)" id="mwL-k">The Last of Us</a></i>, <i id="mwL-o"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Succession_(TV_series)" title="Succession (TV series)" id="mwL-s">Succession</a></i>, <i id="mwL-w"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heated_Rivalry" title="Heated Rivalry" id="mwL-0">Heated Rivalry</a></i> and <i id="mwL-4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger_King" title="Tiger King" id="mwL-8">Tiger King</a></i> gained popularity. Many different shows on many different competing streaming services resulted in what has been called the "streaming wars" of the early 2020s. Miniseries also gained popularity such as <i id="mwL_A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Queen's_Gambit_(miniseries)" title="The Queen's Gambit (miniseries)" id="mwL_E">The Queen's Gambit</a></i>, <i id="mwL_I"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dahmer_–_Monster:_The_Jeffrey_Dahmer_Story" title="Dahmer – Monster: The Jeffrey Dahmer Story" class="mw-redirect" id="mwL_M">Dahmer – Monster: The Jeffrey Dahmer Story</a></i>, <i id="mwL_Q"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daisy_Jones_&amp;_the_Six" title="Daisy Jones &amp; the Six" id="mwL_U">Daisy Jones &amp; the Six</a></i>, <i id="mwL_Y">Beef</i>, <i id="mwL_c"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mr_Bates_vs_The_Post_Office" title="Mr Bates vs The Post Office" id="mwL_g">Mr Bates vs The Post Office</a></i>, <i id="mwL_k"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mrs._America_(miniseries)" title="Mrs. America (miniseries)" id="mwL_o">Mrs. America</a></i>, <i id="mwL_s"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mare_of_Easttown" title="Mare of Easttown" id="mwL_w">Mare of Easttown</a></i>, and <i id="mwL_0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pam_&amp;_Tommy" title="Pam &amp; Tommy" id="mwL_4">Pam &amp; Tommy</a></i>.<sup about="#mwt3744" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1009" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-1009&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-1009" id="mwL_8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMAA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMAE">[</span>1009<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMAI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwMAM">Also released in the 2020s, the reality game show <i id="mwMAQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Traitors" title="The Traitors" id="mwMAU">The Traitors</a></i> achieved popularity and became a global success.<sup about="#mwt3747" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1010" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-1010&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-1010" id="mwMAY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMAc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMAg">[</span>1010<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMAk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt3750" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1011" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-1011&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-1011" id="mwMAo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMAs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMAw">[</span>1011<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMA0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwMA4">Several TV shows based on films include <i id="mwMA8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Gigolo_(TV_series)" title="American Gigolo (TV series)" id="mwMBA">American Gigolo</a></i>, <i id="mwMBE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Penguin_(TV_series)" title="The Penguin (TV series)" id="mwMBI">The Penguin</a></i>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Star_Wars_television_series" title="List of Star Wars television series" id="mwMBM">live-action <i id="mwMBQ">Star Wars</i> series</a> (such as <i id="mwMBU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mandalorian" title="The Mandalorian" id="mwMBY">The Mandalorian</a></i>, <i id="mwMBc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Wars:_Ahsoka" title="Star Wars: Ahsoka" id="mwMBg">Ahsoka</a></i>, and <i id="mwMBk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andor" title="Andor" id="mwMBo">Andor</a></i>), <i id="mwMBs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peacemaker_(TV_series)" title="Peacemaker (TV series)" id="mwMBw">Peacemaker</a></i>, <i id="mwMB0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mr._&amp;_Mrs._Smith_(2024_TV_series)" title="Mr. &amp; Mrs. Smith (2024 TV series)" id="mwMB4">Mr. &amp; Mrs. Smith</a></i>, and <i id="mwMB8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ted_(TV_series)" title="Ted (TV series)" id="mwMCA">Ted</a></i>.</p>
