<li about="#cite_note-no_term_end-237" id="cite_note-no_term_end-237" data-mw-footnote-number="237"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPKc"><a href="#cite_ref-no_term_end_237-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPKg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPKk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-no_term_end-237" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt838" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPKo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;last&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;d'Istria&quot;},&quot;first&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Thomas&quot;},&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;23 May 2024&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Volodymyr Zelensky, a president with no term end&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2024/05/23/volodymyr-zelensky-a-president-with-no-term-end_6672475_4.html&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2 June 2024&quot;},&quot;work&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Le Monde&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFd'Istria2024" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt838">d'Istria, Thomas (23 May 2024). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2024/05/23/volodymyr-zelensky-a-president-with-no-term-end_6672475_4.html" class="external text" id="mwPKs">"Volodymyr Zelensky, a president with no term end"</a>. <i id="mwPKw">Le Monde</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPK0">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPK4">2 June</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Le+Monde&amp;rft.atitle=Volodymyr+Zelensky%2C+a+president+with+no+term+end&amp;rft.date=2024-05-23&amp;rft.aulast=d%27Istria&amp;rft.aufirst=Thomas&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lemonde.fr%2Fen%2Finternational%2Farticle%2F2024%2F05%2F23%2Fvolodymyr-zelensky-a-president-with-no-term-end_6672475_4.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt838" id="mwPK8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-238" id="cite_note-238" data-mw-footnote-number="238"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPLA"><a href="#cite_ref-238" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPLE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPLI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-238" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt841" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPLM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;last1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Oliynyk&quot;},&quot;first1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Tetyana&quot;},&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2 January 2025&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Zelenskyy to decide on second term based on war's outcome&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.pravda.com.ua/eng/news/2025/01/2/7491800/&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;4 January 2025&quot;},&quot;work&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ukrainska Pravda&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFOliynyk2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt841">Oliynyk, Tetyana (2 January 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.pravda.com.ua/eng/news/2025/01/2/7491800/" class="external text" id="mwPLQ">"Zelenskyy to decide on second term based on war's outcome"</a>. <i id="mwPLU">Ukrainska Pravda</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPLY">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPLc">4 January</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Ukrainska+Pravda&amp;rft.atitle=Zelenskyy+to+decide+on+second+term+based+on+war%27s+outcome&amp;rft.date=2025-01-02&amp;rft.aulast=Oliynyk&amp;rft.aufirst=Tetyana&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.pravda.com.ua%2Feng%2Fnews%2F2025%2F01%2F2%2F7491800%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt841" id="mwPLg"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-239" id="cite_note-239" data-mw-footnote-number="239"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPLk"><a href="#cite_ref-239" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPLo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPLs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-239" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt844" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPLw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;web&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.newstatesman.com/new-statesman-view/2025/01/strange-death-of-centre-right&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=The strange death of the centre right: Moderate conservatives have allowed themselves to be marginalized by their populist rivals.&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=March 15, 2025&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=January 15, 2025&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=Before Labour entered power, shadow cabinet ministers spoke of the prospect of a \&quot;progressive moment\&quot;. The hope was that Keir Starmer and other centre-left leaders would unite in a quasi-reenactment of the late 1990s. That dream died on 6 November 2024 when Donald Trump comfortably defeated Kamala Harris. But it is not only Mr. Trump's victory that is evocative of a reactionary moment. Germany's Olaf Scholz – a close ally of Mr Starmer – lost a vote of confidence last year and [was] defeated by the Christian Democrats in next month's general election. The Social Democrats are not only polling behind their traditional rival but also the far-right AfD.&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;website=The New Statesman&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt844" id="mwPL0"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.newstatesman.com/new-statesman-view/2025/01/strange-death-of-centre-right" class="external text" id="mwPL4">"The strange death of the centre right: Moderate conservatives have allowed themselves to be marginalized by their populist rivals"</a>. <i id="mwPL8">The New Statesman</i>. 15 March 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPMA">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPME">15 January</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPMI">Before Labour entered power, shadow cabinet ministers spoke of the prospect of a "progressive moment". The hope was that Keir Starmer and other centre-left leaders would unite in a quasi-reenactment of the late 1990s. That dream died on 6 November 2024 when Donald Trump comfortably defeated Kamala Harris. But it is not only Mr. Trump's victory that is evocative of a reactionary moment. Germany's Olaf Scholz – a close ally of Mr Starmer – lost a vote of confidence last year and [was] defeated by the Christian Democrats in next month's general election. The Social Democrats are not only polling behind their traditional rival but also the far-right AfD.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+Statesman&amp;rft.atitle=The+strange+death+of+the+centre+right%3A+Moderate+conservatives+have+allowed+themselves+to+be+marginalized+by+their+populist+rivals.&amp;rft.date=2025-03-15&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.newstatesman.com%2Fnew-statesman-view%2F2025%2F01%2Fstrange-death-of-centre-right&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt844" id="mwPMM"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-gap_within_the_gender_gap-240" id="cite_note-gap_within_the_gender_gap-240" data-mw-footnote-number="240"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPMQ"><a href="#cite_ref-gap_within_the_gender_gap_240-0" id="mwPMU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPMY">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-gap_within_the_gender_gap_240-1" id="mwPMc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPMg">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-gap_within_the_gender_gap_240-2" id="mwPMk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPMo">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-gap_within_the_gender_gap-240" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt847" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPMs" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;web&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/elections/steve-kornacki-white-men-white-women-gap-gender-gap-rcna196791&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Steve Kornacki: White men, white women, and the gap within the gender gap&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=New NBC News polling data illustrates the cultural and political gulf separating white men without college degrees and white women with college degrees. ... On one end are white men without four-year college degrees. This is a generally blue-collar demographic that is now deeply aligned with Trump and opposed to progressive politics. On the other end are white women with at least four-year college degrees. This is a more affluent demographic that has been racing leftward, particularly on cultural issues, and is squarely opposed to Trump. ... Of course, there are plenty of white voters who do not fall into either of these categories. As groups, college-educated white men and non-college-educated white women lack similarly sharp political definition and cohesion.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Steve&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Kornacki&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;publisher=NBC News&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=March 18, 2025&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=March 19, 2025&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFKornacki2025" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt847">Kornacki, Steve (18 March 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/elections/steve-kornacki-white-men-white-women-gap-gender-gap-rcna196791" class="external text" id="mwPMw">"Steve Kornacki: White men, white women, and the gap within the gender gap"</a>. NBC News<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPM0">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPM4">19 March</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPM8">New NBC News polling data illustrates the cultural and political gulf separating white men without college degrees and white women with college degrees. ... On one end are white men without four-year college degrees. This is a generally blue-collar demographic that is now deeply aligned with Trump and opposed to progressive politics. On the other end are white women with at least four-year college degrees. This is a more affluent demographic that has been racing leftward, particularly on cultural issues, and is squarely opposed to Trump. ... Of course, there are plenty of white voters who do not fall into either of these categories. As groups, college-educated white men and non-college-educated white women lack similarly sharp political definition and cohesion.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Steve+Kornacki%3A+White+men%2C+white+women%2C+and+the+gap+within+the+gender+gap&amp;rft.pub=NBC+News&amp;rft.date=2025-03-18&amp;rft.aulast=Kornacki&amp;rft.aufirst=Steve&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nbcnews.com%2Fpolitics%2Felections%2Fsteve-kornacki-white-men-white-women-gap-gender-gap-rcna196791&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt847" id="mwPNA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-CNN_2024-241" id="cite_note-CNN_2024-241" data-mw-footnote-number="241"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPNE"><a href="#cite_ref-CNN_2024_241-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPNI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPNM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-CNN_2024-241" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt850" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPNQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;November 6, 2024&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Exit poll results 2024&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.cnn.com/election/2024/exit-polls/national-results/general/president/0&quot;},&quot;url-status&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;live&quot;},&quot;archive-url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://web.archive.org/web/20241105154934/https://www.cnn.com/election/2024/exit-polls/national-results/general/president/0&quot;},&quot;archive-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;November 5, 2024&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;November 6, 2024&quot;},&quot;publisher&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;CNN&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt850" id="mwPNU"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cnn.com/election/2024/exit-polls/national-results/general/president/0" class="external text" id="mwPNY">"Exit poll results 2024"</a>. CNN. 6 November 2024. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20241105154934/https://www.cnn.com/election/2024/exit-polls/national-results/general/president/0" class="external text" id="mwPNc">Archived</a> from the original on 5 November 2024<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPNg">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPNk">6 November</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=Exit+poll+results+2024&amp;rft.date=2024-11-06&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnn.com%2Felection%2F2024%2Fexit-polls%2Fnational-results%2Fgeneral%2Fpresident%2F0&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt850" id="mwPNo"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-242" id="cite_note-242" data-mw-footnote-number="242"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPNs"><a href="#cite_ref-242" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPNw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPN0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-242" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt853" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPN4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2024-11-06&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Trump wins the US Presidency&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://apnews.com/live/trump-harris-election-updates-11-5-2024&quot;},&quot;url-status&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;live&quot;},&quot;archive-url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://web.archive.org/web/20241108182720/https://apnews.com/live/trump-harris-election-updates-11-5-2024&quot;},&quot;archive-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;November 8, 2024&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2024-11-06&quot;},&quot;publisher&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;AP News&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt853" id="mwPN8"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://apnews.com/live/trump-harris-election-updates-11-5-2024" class="external text" id="mwPOA">"Trump wins the US Presidency"</a>. AP News. 6 November 2024. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20241108182720/https://apnews.com/live/trump-harris-election-updates-11-5-2024" class="external text" id="mwPOE">Archived</a> from the original on 8 November 2024<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPOI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPOM">6 November</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+wins+the+US+Presidency&amp;rft.date=2024-11-06&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Flive%2Ftrump-harris-election-updates-11-5-2024&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt853" id="mwPOQ"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-243" id="cite_note-243" data-mw-footnote-number="243"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPOU"><a href="#cite_ref-243" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPOY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPOc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-243" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt856" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPOg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;web&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://luskin.ucla.edu/understanding-europes-political-turmoil&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=July 12, 2024&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;website=UCLA Luskin&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=June 12, 2025&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Understanding Europe's Political Turmoil&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=News organizations covering political upheaval in Europe have turned to the 2024 Berggruen Governance Index (BGI) for a deeper understanding of nations' capacity to meet the needs of their people. PA Media cited the index's finding that \&quot;long-term scars\&quot; caused by austerity and Brexit have stifled economic growth and undermined social cohesion in Britain.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt856" id="mwPOk"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://luskin.ucla.edu/understanding-europes-political-turmoil" class="external text" id="mwPOo">"Understanding Europe's Political Turmoil"</a>. <i id="mwPOs">UCLA Luskin</i>. 12 July 2024<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPOw">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPO0">12 June</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPO4">News organizations covering political upheaval in Europe have turned to the 2024 Berggruen Governance Index (BGI) for a deeper understanding of nations' capacity to meet the needs of their people. PA Media cited the index's finding that "long-term scars" caused by austerity and Brexit have stifled economic growth and undermined social cohesion in Britain.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=UCLA+Luskin&amp;rft.atitle=Understanding+Europe%27s+Political+Turmoil&amp;rft.date=2024-07-12&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fluskin.ucla.edu%2Funderstanding-europes-political-turmoil&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt856" id="mwPO8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Canada_2025-244" id="cite_note-Canada_2025-244" data-mw-footnote-number="244"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPPA"><a href="#cite_ref-Canada_2025_244-0" id="mwPPE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPPI">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Canada_2025_244-1" id="mwPPM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPPQ">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Canada_2025-244" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt859" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPPU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;April 30, 2025&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Canada's new Conservative movement resembles Donald Trump's&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.economist.com/the-americas/2025/04/30/canadas-new-conservative-movement-resembles-donald-trumps&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;May 1, 2025&quot;},&quot;newspaper&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;The Economist&quot;},&quot;quote&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Just as in the United States, working-class and immigrant voters swung right. ... The two best predictors of the margin shift between the major parties are education and immigration. Holding all else constant, the Liberals gained ground relative to the Conservatives in ridings with more university graduates and native-born voters. Conversely, they fell back in places with more foreign-born residents and voters who lack degrees.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt859" id="mwPPY"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.economist.com/the-americas/2025/04/30/canadas-new-conservative-movement-resembles-donald-trumps" class="external text" id="mwPPc">"Canada's new Conservative movement resembles Donald Trump's"</a>. <i id="mwPPg">The Economist</i>. 30 April 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPPk">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPPo">1 May</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPPs">Just as in the United States, working-class and immigrant voters swung right. ... The two best predictors of the margin shift between the major parties are education and immigration. Holding all else constant, the Liberals gained ground relative to the Conservatives in ridings with more university graduates and native-born voters. Conversely, they fell back in places with more foreign-born residents and voters who lack degrees.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Economist&amp;rft.atitle=Canada%27s+new+Conservative+movement+resembles+Donald+Trump%27s&amp;rft.date=2025-04-30&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.economist.com%2Fthe-americas%2F2025%2F04%2F30%2Fcanadas-new-conservative-movement-resembles-donald-trumps&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt859" id="mwPPw"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-245" id="cite_note-245" data-mw-footnote-number="245"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPP0"><a href="#cite_ref-245" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPP4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPP8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-245" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt862" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPQA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;web&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.vox.com/politics/414503/left-materialism-far-right-trump-economic-anxiety&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Why the left gets the far right wrong&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=May 28, 2025&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;website=Vox&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=This is not to deny that voters care about material concerns. It's obvious that inflation was a central reason for Trump's 2024 victory.&amp;nbsp;... This is a fundamentally post material account of far-right politics. It argues that the right wins not by channeling people's displaced economic anger, but by articulating ideas that match their deeply held beliefs, values, and identities.&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=November 18, 2025&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Zack&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Beauchamp&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFBeauchamp2025" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt862">Beauchamp, Zack (28 May 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.vox.com/politics/414503/left-materialism-far-right-trump-economic-anxiety" class="external text" id="mwPQE">"Why the left gets the far right wrong"</a>. <i id="mwPQI">Vox</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPQM">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPQQ">18 November</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPQU">This is not to deny that voters care about material concerns. It's obvious that inflation was a central reason for Trump's 2024 victory.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwPQY">&nbsp;</span>... This is a fundamentally post material account of far-right politics. It argues that the right wins not by channeling people's displaced economic anger, but by articulating ideas that match their deeply held beliefs, values, and identities.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Vox&amp;rft.atitle=Why+the+left+gets+the+far+right+wrong&amp;rft.date=2025-05-28&amp;rft.aulast=Beauchamp&amp;rft.aufirst=Zack&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.vox.com%2Fpolitics%2F414503%2Fleft-materialism-far-right-trump-economic-anxiety&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt862" id="mwPQc"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-246" id="cite_note-246" data-mw-footnote-number="246"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPQg"><a href="#cite_ref-246" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPQk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPQo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-246" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt865" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPQs" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;September 11, 2025&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Is British politics broken? Its centre is cracking&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.economist.com/leaders/2025/09/11/is-british-politics-broken-its-centre-is-cracking&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;September 12, 2025&quot;},&quot;newspaper&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;The Economist&quot;},&quot;quote&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;In fact, the Brexit referendum of 2016 accelerated a trend in which age and education, rather than class, are the best predictors of voting behavior.&amp;nbsp;... This is splitting left-leaning young graduates from right-leaning pensioners.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt865" id="mwPQw"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.economist.com/leaders/2025/09/11/is-british-politics-broken-its-centre-is-cracking" class="external text" id="mwPQ0">"Is British politics broken? Its centre is cracking"</a>. <i id="mwPQ4">The Economist</i>. 11 September 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPQ8">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPRA">12 September</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPRE">In fact, the Brexit referendum of 2016 accelerated a trend in which age and education, rather than class, are the best predictors of voting behavior.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwPRI">&nbsp;</span>... This is splitting left-leaning young graduates from right-leaning pensioners.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Economist&amp;rft.atitle=Is+British+politics+broken%3F+Its+centre+is+cracking&amp;rft.date=2025-09-11&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.economist.com%2Fleaders%2F2025%2F09%2F11%2Fis-british-politics-broken-its-centre-is-cracking&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt865" id="mwPRM"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Starmer_CNBC-247" id="cite_note-Starmer_CNBC-247" data-mw-footnote-number="247"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPRQ"><a href="#cite_ref-Starmer_CNBC_247-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPRU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPRY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Starmer_CNBC-247" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt868" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPRc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite &quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; web &quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Ellyatt &quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Holly &quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=25 May 2025 &quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Starmer has delivered some key wins for the UK recently, so why is he so unpopular? &quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.cnbc.com/2025/05/25/starmer-has-delivered-key-wins-for-the-uk-so-why-is-he-so-unpopular.html &quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=9 August 2025 &quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;work=CNBC&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFEllyatt2025" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt868">Ellyatt, Holly (25 May 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cnbc.com/2025/05/25/starmer-has-delivered-key-wins-for-the-uk-so-why-is-he-so-unpopular.html" class="external text" id="mwPRg">"Starmer has delivered some key wins for the UK recently, so why is he so unpopular?"</a>. <i id="mwPRk">CNBC</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPRo">. Retrieved <span class="