<li about="#cite_note-268" id="cite_note-268" data-mw-footnote-number="268"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPfY"><a href="#cite_ref-268" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPfc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPfg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-268" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt925" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPfk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;last&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Newman&quot;},&quot;first&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Andy&quot;},&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;October 29, 2025&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Would Mamdani Be New York's First Immigrant Mayor? Not by a Long Shot.&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/29/nyregion/nyc-immigrant-mayors-mamdani.html&quot;},&quot;url-status&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;live&quot;},&quot;archive-url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://web.archive.org/web/20251030054838/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/29/nyregion/nyc-immigrant-mayors-mamdani.html&quot;},&quot;archive-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;October 30, 2025&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;January 3, 2026&quot;},&quot;work&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[The New York Times]]&quot;},&quot;language&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFNewman2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt925">Newman, Andy (29 October 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/29/nyregion/nyc-immigrant-mayors-mamdani.html" class="external text" id="mwPfo">"Would Mamdani Be New York's First Immigrant Mayor? Not by a Long Shot"</a>. <i id="mwPfs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times" title="The New York Times" id="mwPfw">The New York Times</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20251030054838/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/29/nyregion/nyc-immigrant-mayors-mamdani.html" class="external text" id="mwPf0">Archived</a> from the original on 30 October 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPf4">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPf8">3 January</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Would+Mamdani+Be+New+York%27s+First+Immigrant+Mayor%3F+Not+by+a+Long+Shot.&amp;rft.date=2025-10-29&amp;rft.aulast=Newman&amp;rft.aufirst=Andy&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F10%2F29%2Fnyregion%2Fnyc-immigrant-mayors-mamdani.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt925" id="mwPgA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-269" id="cite_note-269" data-mw-footnote-number="269"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPgE"><a href="#cite_ref-269" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPgI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPgM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-269" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt928" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPgQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;web&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url= https://www.semafor.com/article/11/08/2024/the-democrats-join-a-long-list-of-global-parties-wrecked-by-post-pandemic-backlash&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=The Democrats join a long list of global parties wrecked by post-pandemic backlash&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Brad&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Glasser&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=Four years after the pandemic, governing dysfunction is the story of almost every democracy on the planet, with few examples defying the trend. On nearly every continent, opposition movements have charged ahead in polls, unseated incumbents or lodged in-some-cases historic election gains against a global backdrop of inflation and agitation.&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;website=Semafor&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=November 8, 2024&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFGlasser2024" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt928">Glasser, Brad (8 November 2024). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.semafor.com/article/11/08/2024/the-democrats-join-a-long-list-of-global-parties-wrecked-by-post-pandemic-backlash" class="external text" id="mwPgU">"The Democrats join a long list of global parties wrecked by post-pandemic backlash"</a>. <i id="mwPgY">Semafor</i>. <q id="mwPgc">Four years after the pandemic, governing dysfunction is the story of almost every democracy on the planet, with few examples defying the trend. On nearly every continent, opposition movements have charged ahead in polls, unseated incumbents or lodged in-some-cases historic election gains against a global backdrop of inflation and agitation.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Semafor&amp;rft.atitle=The+Democrats+join+a+long+list+of+global+parties+wrecked+by+post-pandemic+backlash&amp;rft.date=2024-11-08&amp;rft.aulast=Glasser&amp;rft.aufirst=Brad&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.semafor.com%2Farticle%2F11%2F08%2F2024%2Fthe-democrats-join-a-long-list-of-global-parties-wrecked-by-post-pandemic-backlash&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt928" id="mwPgg"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Gerstle2022-270" id="cite_note-Gerstle2022-270" data-mw-footnote-number="270"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPgk"><a href="#cite_ref-Gerstle2022_270-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPgo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPgs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Gerstle2022-270" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt931" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPgw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;cite book &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_book&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;last&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gerstle&quot;},&quot;first&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gary&quot;},&quot;author-link&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gary Gerstle&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://global.oup.com/academic/product/the-rise-and-fall-of-the-neoliberal-order-9780197519646&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;The Rise and Fall of the Neoliberal Order: America and the World in the Free Market Era&quot;},&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2022&quot;},&quot;publisher&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[Oxford University Press]]&quot;},&quot;isbn&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;978-0-19-751964-6&quot;},&quot;quote&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;The most sweeping account of how neoliberalism came to dominate American politics for nearly a half century before crashing against the forces of Trumpism on the right and a new progressivism on the left.&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;August 1, 2024&quot;},&quot;archive-url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://web.archive.org/web/20220626220259/https://global.oup.com/academic/product/the-rise-and-fall-of-the-neoliberal-order-9780197519646?cc=us&amp;lang=en&amp;&quot;},&quot;archive-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;June 26, 2022&quot;},&quot;url-status&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;live&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFGerstle2022" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt931"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gary_Gerstle" title="Gary Gerstle" id="mwPg0">Gerstle, Gary</a> (2022). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://global.oup.com/academic/product/the-rise-and-fall-of-the-neoliberal-order-9780197519646" class="external text" id="mwPg4"><i id="mwPg8">The Rise and Fall of the Neoliberal Order: America and the World in the Free Market Era</i></a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxford_University_Press" title="Oxford University Press" id="mwPhA">Oxford University Press</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwPhE">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwPhI">&nbsp;</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-19-751964-6" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-19-751964-6" id="mwPhM"><bdi id="mwPhQ">978-0-19-751964-6</bdi></a>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20220626220259/https://global.oup.com/academic/product/the-rise-and-fall-of-the-neoliberal-order-9780197519646?cc=us&amp;lang=en&amp;" class="external text" id="mwPhU">Archived</a> from the original on 26 June 2022<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPhY">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPhc">1 August</span> 2024</span>. <q id="mwPhg">The most sweeping account of how neoliberalism came to dominate American politics for nearly a half century before crashing against the forces of Trumpism on the right and a new progressivism on the left.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=The+Rise+and+Fall+of+the+Neoliberal+Order%3A+America+and+the+World+in+the+Free+Market+Era&amp;rft.pub=Oxford+University+Press&amp;rft.date=2022&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-19-751964-6&amp;rft.aulast=Gerstle&amp;rft.aufirst=Gary&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fglobal.oup.com%2Facademic%2Fproduct%2Fthe-rise-and-fall-of-the-neoliberal-order-9780197519646&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt931" id="mwPhk"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-271" id="cite_note-271" data-mw-footnote-number="271"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPho"><a href="#cite_ref-271" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPhs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPhw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-271" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt934" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPh0" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;last&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Williams&quot;},&quot;first&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Aime&quot;},&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;August 6, 2025&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Donald Trump's new tariff regime deepens global trade war&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.ft.com/content/9f642686-d9bf-4d16-a2f6-2d2ab8fb43d2&quot;},&quot;url-access&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;subscription&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;August 8, 2025&quot;},&quot;work&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Financial Times&quot;},&quot;quote&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Donald Trump's global tariffs took effect at 12.01am in Washington on Thursday, pushing American import duties to their highest level in a century as the US president launched a new era of trade rivalry.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFWilliams2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt934">Williams, Aime (6 August 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwPh4"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.ft.com/content/9f642686-d9bf-4d16-a2f6-2d2ab8fb43d2" class="external text" id="mwPh8">"Donald Trump's new tariff regime deepens global trade war"</a></span>. <i id="mwPiA">Financial Times</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPiE">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPiI">8 August</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPiM">Donald Trump's global tariffs took effect at 12.01am in Washington on Thursday, pushing American import duties to their highest level in a century as the US president launched a new era of trade rivalry.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Financial+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Donald+Trump%27s+new+tariff+regime+deepens+global+trade+war&amp;rft.date=2025-08-06&amp;rft.aulast=Williams&amp;rft.aufirst=Aime&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ft.com%2Fcontent%2F9f642686-d9bf-4d16-a2f6-2d2ab8fb43d2&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt934" id="mwPiQ"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-272" id="cite_note-272" data-mw-footnote-number="272"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPiU"><a href="#cite_ref-272" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPiY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPic">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-272" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt937" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPig" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;last&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Goldman&quot;},&quot;first&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;David&quot;},&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;August 1, 2025&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Trump's new tariffs have no precedent in the modern era&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.cnn.com/2025/08/01/economy/tariff-policy-trump-trade&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;August 8, 2025&quot;},&quot;work&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[CNN]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFGoldman2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt937">Goldman, David (1 August 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cnn.com/2025/08/01/economy/tariff-policy-trump-trade" class="external text" id="mwPik">"Trump's new tariffs have no precedent in the modern era"</a>. <i id="mwPio"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNN" title="CNN" id="mwPis">CNN</a></i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPiw">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPi0">8 August</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=CNN&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+new+tariffs+have+no+precedent+in+the+modern+era&amp;rft.date=2025-08-01&amp;rft.aulast=Goldman&amp;rft.aufirst=David&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnn.com%2F2025%2F08%2F01%2Feconomy%2Ftariff-policy-trump-trade&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt937" id="mwPi4"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-273" id="cite_note-273" data-mw-footnote-number="273"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPi8"><a href="#cite_ref-273" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPjA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPjE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-273" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt940" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPjI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;last&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Romm&quot;},&quot;first&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Tony&quot;},&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;August 7, 2025&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Staggering U.S. Tariffs Begin as Trump Widens Trade War&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/2025/08/07/business/economy/trump-tariffs-trade-war.html&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;August 9, 2025&quot;},&quot;work&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[The New York Times]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFRomm2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt940">Romm, Tony (7 August 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/08/07/business/economy/trump-tariffs-trade-war.html" class="external text" id="mwPjM">"Staggering U.S. Tariffs Begin as Trump Widens Trade War"</a>. <i id="mwPjQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times" title="The New York Times" id="mwPjU">The New York Times</a></i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPjY">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPjc">9 August</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Staggering+U.S.+Tariffs+Begin+as+Trump+Widens+Trade+War&amp;rft.date=2025-08-07&amp;rft.aulast=Romm&amp;rft.aufirst=Tony&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F08%2F07%2Fbusiness%2Feconomy%2Ftrump-tariffs-trade-war.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt940" id="mwPjg"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Well-to-Do-274" id="cite_note-Well-to-Do-274" data-mw-footnote-number="274"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPjk"><a href="#cite_ref-Well-to-Do_274-0" id="mwPjo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPjs">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Well-to-Do_274-1" id="mwPjw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPj0">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Well-to-Do-274" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt960" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPj4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;web&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/23/opinion/democrats-rich-poor.html&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=By 2024, the realignment of income and political party was complete. Americans with more money voted for Kamala Harris while Donald Trump won among the working class.&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=October 23, 2025&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=October 23, 2025&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=How Democrats Became the Party of the Well-to-Do&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;website=The New York Times&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Brody&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Williams&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="mwPj8" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt960" data-x-id="CITEREFWilliams2025">Williams, Brody (23 October 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/23/opinion/democrats-rich-poor.html" class="external text" id="mwPkA">"How Democrats Became the Party of the Well-to-Do"</a>. <i id="mwPkE">The New York Times</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPkI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPkM">23 October</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPkQ">By 2024, the realignment of income and political party was complete. Americans with more money voted for Kamala Harris while Donald Trump won among the working class.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=How+Democrats+Became+the+Party+of+the+Well-to-Do&amp;rft.date=2025-10-23&amp;rft.aulast=Williams&amp;rft.aufirst=Brody&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F10%2F23%2Fopinion%2Fdemocrats-rich-poor.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt960" id="mwPkU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-275" id="cite_note-275" data-mw-footnote-number="275"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPkY"><a href="#cite_ref-275" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPkc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPkg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-275" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt944" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPkk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;web&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2025/01/biden-economic-populism-failure/681289/&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Maybe It Was Never About the Factory Jobs&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=January 13, 2025&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=January 15, 2025&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=The theory that populist economic policies can win back the working class for Democrats has been tried, and it has failed.&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Jonathan&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Chait&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;website=The Atlantic&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFChait2025" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt944">Chait, Jonathan (13 January 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2025/01/biden-economic-populism-failure/681289/" class="external text" id="mwPko">"Maybe It Was Never About the Factory Jobs"</a>. <i id="mwPks">The Atlantic</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPkw">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPk0">15 January</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPk4">The theory that populist economic policies can win back the working class for Democrats has been tried, and it has failed.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Atlantic&amp;rft.atitle=Maybe+It+Was+Never+About+the+Factory+Jobs&amp;rft.date=2025-01-13&amp;rft.aulast=Chait&amp;rft.aufirst=Jonathan&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theatlantic.com%2Fideas%2Farchive%2F2025%2F01%2Fbiden-economic-populism-failure%2F681289%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt944" id="mwPk8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-276" id="cite_note-276" data-mw-footnote-number="276"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPlA"><a href="#cite_ref-276" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPlE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPlI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-276" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt947" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPlM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;May 29, 2021&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Educated voters' leftward shift is surprisingly old and international&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.economist.com/graphic-detail/2021/05/29/educated-voters-leftward-shift-is-surprisingly-old-and-international&quot;},&quot;newspaper&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;The Economist&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt947" id="mwPlQ"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.economist.com/graphic-detail/2021/05/29/educated-voters-leftward-shift-is-surprisingly-old-and-international" class="external text" id="mwPlU">"Educated voters' leftward shift is surprisingly old and international"</a>. <i id="mwPlY">The Economist</i>. 29 May 2021.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Economist&amp;rft.atitle=Educated+voters%27+leftward+shift+is+surprisingly+old+and+international&amp;rft.date=2021-05-29&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.economist.com%2Fgraphic-detail%2F2021%2F05%2F29%2Feducated-voters-leftward-shift-is-surprisingly-old-and-international&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt947" id="mwPlc"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-277" id="cite_note-277" data-mw-footnote-number="277"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPlg"><a href="#cite_ref-277" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPlk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPlo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-277" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt951" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPls" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;September 11, 2025&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Labour has become the Party of Britain's rich&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.economist.com/britain/2025/09/11/labour-has-become-the-party-of-britains-rich&quot;},&quot;newspaper&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;The Economist&quot;},&quot;quote&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;This is the first such study conducted since [the] hard-right Reform UK party surged into first place in polls earlier this year. ... The party is particularly popular with older voters and those who did not attend university. Less than one in 20 supporters are non-white ... and 57% are men.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt951" id="mwPlw"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.economist.com/britain/2025/09/11/labour-has-become-the-party-of-britains-rich" class="external text" id="mwPl0">"Labour has become the Party of Britain's rich"</a>. <i id="mwPl4">The Economist</i>. 11 September 2025. <q id="mwPl8">This is the first such study conducted since [the] hard-right Reform UK party surged into first place in polls earlier this year. ... The party is particularly popular with older voters and those who did not attend university. Less than one in 20 supporters are non-white ... and 57% are men.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Economist&amp;rft.atitle=Labour+has+become+the+Party+of+Britain%27s+rich&amp;rft.date=2025-09-11&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.economist.com%2Fbritain%2F2025%2F09%2F11%2Flabour-has-become-the-party-of-britains-rich&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt951" id="mwPmA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-278" id="cite_note-278" data-mw-footnote-number="278"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPmE"><a href="#cite_ref-278" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPmI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPmM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-278" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt954" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPmQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;web&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-us-expansion-talk-canada-greenland-politics-desk-rcna186713&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=The parts of the country that have seen the biggest political shifts during the Trump era&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=Here are the 25 counties that have moved toward the Republican Party by the largest margins during the Trump era. ... Starr and Elliott both embody one of the two demographic features common to all 25 of those GOP-trending counties. [Ten] counties on the list also have majority-Hispanic populations, with concentrations from 51% to 95%. That basic profile also fits [fifteen] other counties on the list — heavily white and blue-collar. ... At the other end of the spectrum, there are the 25 areas that have moved the most decisively toward Democrats during the Trump era. ... The remaining 16 counties on the list stand out for two reasons. One is their wealth. Eleven of them feature six-figure median household incomes. ... Those 16 places also have large populations of white residents with four-year college degrees.&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;website=NBC News&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Steve&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Kornacki&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=January 7, 2025&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=November 13, 2025&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="mwPmU" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt954" data-x-id="CITEREFKornacki2025">Kornacki, Steve (7 January 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-us-expansion-talk-canada-greenland-politics-desk-rcna186713" class="external text" id="mwPmY">"The parts of the country that have seen the biggest political shifts during the Trump era"</a>. <i id="mwPmc">NBC News</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPmg">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPmk">13 November</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPmo">Here are the 25 counties that have moved toward the Republican Party by the largest margins during the Trump era. ... Starr and Elliott both embody one of the two demographic features common to all 25 of those GOP-trending counties. [Ten] counties on the list also have majority-Hispanic populations, with concentrations from 51% to 95%. That basic profile also fits [fifteen] other counties on the list — heavily white and blue-collar. ... At the other end of the spectrum, there are the 25 areas that have moved the most decisively toward Democrats during the Trump era. ... The remaining 16 counties on the list stand out for two reasons. One is their wealth. Eleven of them feature six-figure median household incomes. ... Those 16 places also have large populations of white residents with four-year college degrees.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=NBC+News&amp;rft.atitle=The+parts+of+the+country+that+have+seen+the+biggest+political+shifts+during+the+Trump+era&amp;rft.date=2025-01-07&amp;rft.aulast=Kornacki&amp;rft.aufirst=Steve&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nbcnews.com%2Fpolitics%2Ftrump-us-expansion-talk-canada-greenland-politics-desk-rcna186713&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt954" id="mwPms"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-279" id="cite_note-279" data-mw-footnote-number="279"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPmw"><a href="#cite_ref-279" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPm0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPm4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-279" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt957" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPm8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;web&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=http://piketty.pse.ens.fr/files/Piketty2018PSEPoliticalConflict.pdf&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=High-education &amp; high-income voters might also unite in the future, giving rise to a complete realignment of the party system: globalists (high-education, high-income) vs nativists (low-education, low-income). Like in post-communist Europe?&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=20 March 2018&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=13 November 2025&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Thomas&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Piketty&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Brahmin Left vs Merchant Right: Rising Inequality and the Changing Structure of Political Conflict&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFPiketty2018" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt957">Piketty, Thomas (20 March 2018). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://piketty.pse.ens.fr/files/Piketty2018PSEPoliticalConflict.pdf" class="external text" id="mwPnA">"Brahmin Left vs Merchant Right: Rising Inequality and the Changing Structure of Political Conflict"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwPnE">(PDF)</span><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPnI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPnM">13 November</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPnQ">High-education &amp; high-income voters might also unite in the future, giving rise to a complete realignment of the party system: globalists (high-education, high-income) vs nativists (low-education, low-income). Like in post-communist Europe?</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Brahmin+Left+vs+Merchant+Right%3A+Rising+Inequality+and+the+Changing+Structure+of+Political+Conflict&amp;rft.date=2018-03-20&amp;rft.aulast=Piketty&amp;rft.aufirst=Thomas&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fpiketty.pse.ens.fr%2Ffiles%2FPiketty2018PSEPoliticalConflict.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt957" id="mwPnU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Hispanic_men,_white_women-280" id="cite_note-Hispanic_men,_white_women-280" data-mw-footnote-number="280"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPnY"><a href="#cite_ref-Hispanic_men,_white_women_280-0" id="mwPnc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPng">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Hispanic_men,_white_women_280-1" id="mwPnk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPno">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Hispanic_men,_white_women-280" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt964" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPns" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite&quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;web&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-gains-with-hispanic-men-harris-up-with-white-women-reutersipsos-polls-show-2024-10-25/ &quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Trump gains with Hispanic men, Harris up with white women, Reuters/Ipsos polls show&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=October 28, 2024&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;website=Reuters&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=October 28, 2024&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Jason&quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Lange&quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first2=Bo&quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last2=Erickson&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFLangeErickson2024" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt964">Lange, Jason; Erickson, Bo (28 October 2024). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-gains-with-hispanic-men-harris-up-with-white-women-reutersipsos-polls-show-2024-10-25/" class="external text" id="mwPnw">"Trump gains with Hispanic men, Harris up with white women, Reuters/Ipsos polls show"</a>. <i id="mwPn0">Reuters</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPn4">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPn8">28 October</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Reuters&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+gains+with+Hispanic+men%2C+Harris+up+with+white+women%2C+Reuters%2FIpsos+polls+show&amp;rft.date=2024-10-28&amp;rft.aulast=Lange&amp;rft.aufirst=Jason&amp;rft.au=Erickson%2C+Bo&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.reuters.com%2Fworld%2Fus%2Ftrump-gains-with-hispanic-men-harris-up-with-white-women-reutersipsos-polls-show-2024-10-25%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt964" id="mwPoA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-281" id="cite_note-281" data-mw-footnote-number="281"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPoE"><a href="#cite_ref-281" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPoI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPoM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-281" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt969" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPoQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;last&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Hirsch&quot;},&quot;first&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Michael&quot;},&quot;author-link&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Michael Hirsh (journalist)&quot;},&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;12 March 2022&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Putin's Thousand-Year War&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://foreignpolicy.com/2022/03/12/putins-thousand-year-war/&quot;},&quot;work&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[Foreign Policy]]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFHirsch2022" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt969"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Hirsh_(journalist)" title="Michael Hirsh (journalist)" id="mwPoU">Hirsch, Michael</a> (12 March 2022). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://foreignpolicy.com/2022/03/12/putins-thousand-year-war/" class="external text" id="mwPoY">"Putin's Thousand-Year War"</a>. <i id="mwPoc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_Policy" title="Foreign Policy" id="mwPog">Foreign Policy</a></i>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Foreign+Policy&amp;rft.atitle=Putin%27s+Thousand-Year+War&amp;rft.date=2022-03-12&amp;rft.aulast=Hirsch&amp;rft.aufirst=Michael&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fforeignpolicy.com%2F2022%2F03%2F12%2Fputins-thousand-year-war%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt969" id="mwPok"></span></span></li>
