<li about="#cite_note-283" id="cite_note-283" data-mw-footnote-number="283"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPpM"><a href="#cite_ref-283" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPpQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPpU">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-283" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt975" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPpY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Cite book &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_book&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;last1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;McFaul&quot;},&quot;first1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Michael&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://books.google.com/books?id=0n72EAAAQBAJ&amp;dq=On+February+24,+2022,+Russian+president+Vladimir+Putin+launched+a+full-+scale+invasion+of+Ukraine,+expanding+dramatically+the+war+against+Ukraine+he+be+gan+in+2014+and+starting+the+largest+war+in+Europe+since+World+War+II.&amp;pg=PA34&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;War in Ukraine: Conflict, Strategy, and the Return of a Fractured World&quot;},&quot;last2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Person&quot;},&quot;first2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Robert&quot;},&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2 April 2024&quot;},&quot;publisher&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[Johns Hopkins University Press]]&quot;},&quot;isbn&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;978-1-4214-4985-2&quot;},&quot;editor1-last&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Brands&quot;},&quot;editor1-first&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Hal&quot;},&quot;page&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;34&quot;},&quot;language&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;en&quot;},&quot;quote&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;On February 24, 2022, Russian president Vladimir Putin launched a full-scale invasion of Ukraine, expanding dramatically the war against Ukraine he began in 2014 and starting the largest war in Europe since World War II.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFMcFaulPerson2024" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt975">McFaul, Michael; Person, Robert (2 April 2024). Brands, Hal (ed.). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=0n72EAAAQBAJ&amp;dq=On+February+24,+2022,+Russian+president+Vladimir+Putin+launched+a+full-+scale+invasion+of+Ukraine,+expanding+dramatically+the+war+against+Ukraine+he+be+gan+in+2014+and+starting+the+largest+war+in+Europe+since+World+War+II.&amp;pg=PA34" class="external text" id="mwPpc"><i id="mwPpg">War in Ukraine: Conflict, Strategy, and the Return of a Fractured World</i></a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johns_Hopkins_University_Press" title="Johns Hopkins University Press" id="mwPpk">Johns Hopkins University Press</a>. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwPpo">&nbsp;</span>34. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwPps">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwPpw">&nbsp;</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-1-4214-4985-2" title="Special:BookSources/978-1-4214-4985-2" id="mwPp0"><bdi id="mwPp4">978-1-4214-4985-2</bdi></a>. <q id="mwPp8">On February 24, 2022, Russian president Vladimir Putin launched a full-scale invasion of Ukraine, expanding dramatically the war against Ukraine he began in 2014 and starting the largest war in Europe since World War II.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=War+in+Ukraine%3A+Conflict%2C+Strategy%2C+and+the+Return+of+a+Fractured+World&amp;rft.pages=34&amp;rft.pub=Johns+Hopkins+University+Press&amp;rft.date=2024-04-02&amp;rft.isbn=978-1-4214-4985-2&amp;rft.aulast=McFaul&amp;rft.aufirst=Michael&amp;rft.au=Person%2C+Robert&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3D0n72EAAAQBAJ%26dq%3DOn%2BFebruary%2B24%2C%2B2022%2C%2BRussian%2Bpresident%2BVladimir%2BPutin%2Blaunched%2Ba%2Bfull-%2Bscale%2Binvasion%2Bof%2BUkraine%2C%2Bexpanding%2Bdramatically%2Bthe%2Bwar%2Bagainst%2BUkraine%2Bhe%2Bbe%2Bgan%2Bin%2B2014%2Band%2Bstarting%2Bthe%2Blargest%2Bwar%2Bin%2BEurope%2Bsince%2BWorld%2BWar%2BII.%26pg%3DPA34&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt975" id="mwPqA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Global_Divide-284" id="cite_note-Global_Divide-284" data-mw-footnote-number="284"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPqE"><a href="#cite_ref-Global_Divide_284-0" id="mwPqI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPqM">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Global_Divide_284-1" id="mwPqQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPqU">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Global_Divide-284" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt978" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPqY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite &quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; web &quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last1=Higgins &quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first1=Andrew &quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=June 2, 2025 &quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Caught Between Two Wests: New Global Divide Runs Straight Through Poland &quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/02/world/europe/poland-president-election-results.html &quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=July 23, 2025 &quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;website=The New York Times &quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=The country's government is centrist, with deep ties to Brussels. Its new president is a Trump-backed nationalist. That reflects a broader struggle. ... Battles have raged over divisive issues like migration, abortion, and LGBT rights. ... No longer united by faith in a single model, Poland and other countries on the European Union's eastern flank now find themselves caught between the populist nationalism of Mr. Trump and defenders of the old post-Cold War liberal order.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFHiggins2025" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt978">Higgins, Andrew (2 June 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/02/world/europe/poland-president-election-results.html" class="external text" id="mwPqc">"Caught Between Two Wests: New Global Divide Runs Straight Through Poland"</a>. <i id="mwPqg">The New York Times</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPqk">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPqo">23 July</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPqs">The country's government is centrist, with deep ties to Brussels. Its new president is a Trump-backed nationalist. That reflects a broader struggle. ... Battles have raged over divisive issues like migration, abortion, and LGBT rights. ... No longer united by faith in a single model, Poland and other countries on the European Union's eastern flank now find themselves caught between the populist nationalism of Mr. Trump and defenders of the old post-Cold War liberal order.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Caught+Between+Two+Wests%3A+New+Global+Divide+Runs+Straight+Through+Poland&amp;rft.date=2025-06-02&amp;rft.aulast=Higgins&amp;rft.aufirst=Andrew&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F06%2F02%2Fworld%2Feurope%2Fpoland-president-election-results.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt978" id="mwPqw"></span></span></li>
