<li about="#cite_note-Beauchamp_2024-293" id="cite_note-Beauchamp_2024-293" data-mw-footnote-number="293"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPwE"><a href="#cite_ref-Beauchamp_2024_293-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPwI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPwM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Beauchamp_2024-293" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1008" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPwQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite &quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; web &quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;last=Beauchamp &quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;first=Zack &quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;date=17 July 2024 &quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Why the far right is surging all over the world &quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://www.vox.com/politics/361136/far-right-authoritarianism-germany-reactionary-spirit &quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=8 August 2025 &quot;},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;website=Vox &quot;},&quot;9&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;archive-date=17 July 2024 &quot;},&quot;10&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240717102105/https://www.vox.com/politics/361136/far-right-authoritarianism-germany-reactionary-spirit &quot;},&quot;11&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url-status=live&quot;},&quot;12&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=But its rise illustrates something vitally important: That Germany, of all countries, could fail to prevent a surge in reactionary and antidemocratic politics suggests there's something eternal and enduring about the reactionary spirit.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFBeauchamp2024" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt1008">Beauchamp, Zack (17 July 2024). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.vox.com/politics/361136/far-right-authoritarianism-germany-reactionary-spirit" class="external text" id="mwPwU">"Why the far right is surging all over the world"</a>. <i id="mwPwY">Vox</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20240717102105/https://www.vox.com/politics/361136/far-right-authoritarianism-germany-reactionary-spirit" class="external text" id="mwPwc">Archived</a> from the original on 17 July 2024<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPwg">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPwk">8 August</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwPwo">But its rise illustrates something vitally important: That Germany, of all countries, could fail to prevent a surge in reactionary and antidemocratic politics suggests there's something eternal and enduring about the reactionary spirit.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Vox&amp;rft.atitle=Why+the+far+right+is+surging+all+over+the+world&amp;rft.date=2024-07-17&amp;rft.aulast=Beauchamp&amp;rft.aufirst=Zack&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.vox.com%2Fpolitics%2F361136%2Ffar-right-authoritarianism-germany-reactionary-spirit&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1008" id="mwPws"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-graveyard-294" id="cite_note-graveyard-294" data-mw-footnote-number="294"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPww"><a href="#cite_ref-graveyard_294-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPw0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPw4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-graveyard-294" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1011" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPw8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;last&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Burn-Murdoch&quot;},&quot;first&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;John&quot;},&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;November 7, 2024&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Democrats join 2024's graveyard of incumbents&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.ft.com/content/e8ac09ea-c300-4249-af7d-109003afb893&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;November 8, 2024&quot;},&quot;work&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Financial Times&quot;},&quot;quote&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;That different politicians, different parties, different policies and different rhetoric deployed in different countries have all met similar fortunes suggests that a large part of Tuesday's American result was locked in regardless of the messenger or the message. The wide variety of places and people who swung towards Trump also suggests an outcome that was more inevitable than contingent.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id="CITEREFBurn-Murdoch2024" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1011">Burn-Murdoch, John (7 November 2024). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.ft.com/content/e8ac09ea-c300-4249-af7d-109003afb893" class="external text" id="mwPxA">"Democrats join 2024's graveyard of incumbents"</a>. <i id="mwPxE">Financial Times</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPxI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPxM">8 November</span> 2024</span>. <q id="mwPxQ">That different politicians, different parties, different policies and different rhetoric deployed in different countries have all met similar fortunes suggests that a large part of Tuesday's American result was locked in regardless of the messenger or the message. The wide variety of places and people who swung towards Trump also suggests an outcome that was more inevitable than contingent.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Financial+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Democrats+join+2024%27s+graveyard+of+incumbents&amp;rft.date=2024-11-07&amp;rft.aulast=Burn-Murdoch&amp;rft.aufirst=John&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ft.com%2Fcontent%2Fe8ac09ea-c300-4249-af7d-109003afb893&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1011" id="mwPxU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-295" id="cite_note-295" data-mw-footnote-number="295"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwPxY"><a href="#cite_ref-295" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwPxc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwPxg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-295" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1014" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwPxk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Cite web &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_web&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2020-12-29&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Ten World Figures Who Died in 2020 {{!}} Council on Foreign Relations&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.cfr.org/articles/ten-world-figures-who-died-2020&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2026-06-06&quot;},&quot;website&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;www.cfr.org&quot;},&quot;language&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt1014" id="mwPxo"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cfr.org/articles/ten-world-figures-who-died-2020" class="external text" id="mwPxs">"Ten World Figures Who Died in 2020 | Council on Foreign Relations"</a>. <i id="mwPxw">www.cfr.org</i>. 29 December 2020<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwPx0">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwPx4">6 June</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=www.cfr.org&amp;rft.atitle=Ten+World+Figures+Who+Died+in+2020+%7C+Council+on+Foreign+Relations&amp;rft.date=2020-12-29&amp;rf