2030 – UN report"</a>. <i id="mwWes">Reuters</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwWew">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwWe0">31 October</span> 2022</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Reuters&amp;rft.atitle=COP27%3A+World+on+track+to+increase+emissions+10.6%25+by+2030+%E2%80%93+UN+report&amp;rft.date=2022-10-26&amp;rft.aulast=Dickie&amp;rft.aufirst=Gloria&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.reuters.com%2Fbusiness%2Fenvironment%2Fcop27-world-track-increase-emissions-106-by-2030-un-report-2022-10-26%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3576" id="mwWe4"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-959" id="cite_note-959" data-mw-footnote-number="959"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwWe8"><a href="#cite_ref-959" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwWfA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwWfE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-959" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3579" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwWfI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#invoke:cite &quot;,&quot;function&quot;:&quot;invoke&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot; web &quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;title=Nationally determined contributions under the Paris Agreement. Synthesis report by the secretariat &quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;url=https://unfccc.int/documents/619180 &quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;website=unfccc.int &quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;access-date=31 October 2022 &quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;quote=In the context of the carbon budget consistent with 50 per cent likelihood of limiting warming to 1.5 °C (500 Gt CO2), cumulative CO2 emissions in 2020–2030 based on the latest NDCs would likely use up 86 per cent of the remaining carbon budget, leaving a post-2030 carbon budget of around 70 Gt CO2, which is equivalent to approximately two years of projected total global CO2 emissions by 2030.&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt3579" id="mwWfM"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://unfccc.int/documents/619180" class="external text" id="mwWfQ">"Nationally determined contributions under the Paris Agreement. Synthesis report by the secretariat"</a>. <i id="mwWfU">unfccc.int</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwWfY">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwWfc">31 October</span> 2022</span>. <q id="mwWfg">In the context of the carbon budget consistent with 50 per cent likelihood of limiting warming to 1.5 °C (500 Gt CO2), cumulative CO2 emissions in 2020–2030 based on the latest NDCs would likely use up 86 per cent of the remaining carbon budget, leaving a post-2030 carbon budget of around 70 Gt CO2, which is equivalent to approximately two years of projected total global CO2 emissions by 2030.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=unfccc.int&amp;rft.atitle=Nationally+determined+contributions+under+the+Paris+Agreement.+Synthesis+report+by+the+secretariat&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Funfccc.int%2Fdocuments%2F619180&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2020s" class="Z3988" about="#mwt3579" id="mwWfk"></span>
